<h2>Breaking Changes</h2>

<p><strong>Important:</strong> These changes may require updates to existing workflows:</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>Git Operations</strong>: Git functionality moved from Admin controller to dedicated Admin::Git controller</li>
<li><strong>Authentication</strong>: Enhanced authentication requirements for admin functions</li>
<li><strong>Template Format</strong>: AI guidelines converted from .tt to .md format (affects documentation system)</li>
</ul>

<h2>Benefits</h2>

<ul>
<li><strong>Improved Security</strong>: Centralized authentication system with better session management</li>
<li><strong>Better Organization</strong>: Dedicated controllers for specific functionality</li>
<li><strong>Enhanced Maintainability</strong>: Cleaner code structure and better separation of concerns</li>
<li><strong>Improved Documentation</strong>: Better documentation management and organization</li>
<li><strong>Enhanced Deployment</strong>: Better deployment procedures and infrastructure</li>
</ul>

<h2>Next Steps</h2>

<ol>
<li><strong>Testing</strong>: Thoroughly test all Git operations through the new Admin::Git controller</li>
<li><strong>Documentation Review</strong>: Review all documentation for accuracy and completeness</li>
<li><strong>User Training</strong>: Update user documentation for new Git management interface</li>
<li><strong>Performance Monitoring</strong>: Monitor system performance with new enhancements</li>
</ol>

<h2>Related Documentation</h2>

