    <div class="doc-section">
        <h2>Technical Changes</h2>
        
        <h3>Controller Updates</h3>
        <pre class="code-block">
# Enhanced role-based access control logic
if (lc($role) eq lc($user_role)) {
    $has_role = 1;
    $self->logging->log_with_details($c, 'debug', __FILE__, __LINE__, 'view',
        "Role match: user role $user_role matches required role $role for page $page");
    last;
}
# Special case for normal role - any authenticated user can access normal content
elsif (lc($role) eq 'normal' && $user_role) {
    $has_role = 1;
    $self->logging->log_with_details($c, 'debug', __FILE__, __LINE__, 'view',
        "Normal role access granted to page $page for user with role $user_role");
    last;
}
        </pre>
        
        <h3>Path Resolution Logic</h3>
        <pre class="code-block">
# Check if there's a default path defined in the documentation_config.json file
if ($config->{default_paths} && $config->{default_paths}{$page}) {
    $default_path = $config->{default_paths}{$page};
    $self->logging->log_with_details($c, 'info', __FILE__, __LINE__, 'view',
        "Found default path for $page: $default_path");
}

# If a default path is defined, try to use it
if ($default_path) {
    my $full_default_path = $c->path_to('root', $default_path);
    
    if (-e $full_default_path) {
        $self->logging->log_with_details($c, 'info', __FILE__, __LINE__, 'view',
            "Using default path for $page: $default_path");
            
        # Determine file type based on extension and render appropriately
        # ...
    }
}
        </pre>
    </div>
    
    <div class="doc-section">
        <h2>User Impact</h2>
        <p>
            These changes improve the documentation system in the following ways:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Normal users can now access all documentation intended for them</li>
            <li>Documentation pages are properly rendered with consistent styling</li>
            <li>Error messages are more informative and helpful</li>
            <li>Navigation between documentation pages is more reliable</li>
            <li>Role-based access control works correctly for all user types</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
    
    <div class="doc-section">
        <h2>Related Documentation</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/Documentation/documentation_migration_to_tt') %&#93;">Documentation Migration to Template Toolkit</a></li>
            <li><a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/Documentation/documentation_tt_template') %&#93;">Documentation Template Toolkit Template</a></li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="2026-04-28-3d-printing-system" class="cl-entry">
<h3>3D Printing System</h3>
&#91;% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %&#93;&#91;% PageVersion %&#93;&#91;% END %&#93;







<div class="changelog-entry">
    <header class="changelog-header">
        <h1>3D Printing System</h1>
        <div class="changelog-meta">
            <span class="date">April 28, 2026</span>
            <span class="author">by shanta</span>
            <span class="type">New System</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="changelog-summary">
        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <p>New <code>3d</code> controller providing a complete 3D printing management system: STL/OBJ/3MF/GCode file upload with STL geometry parsing, a model library linked to inventory items, a printer farm tracker, a print job queue with consignment integration, and a customer-facing store (unified with the Shop system).</p>
    </section>

    <section class="changelog-details">
        <h2>Routes</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>/3d</code> — index page</li>
            <li><code>/3d/browse</code> — public model browser</li>
            <li><code>/3d/model/&lt;id&gt;</code> — model detail page</li>
            <li><code>/3d/model_download/&lt;id&gt;</code> — download model file</li>
            <li><code>/3d/store</code> — redirects to <code>/shop</code> (unified with Shop system)</li>
            <li><code>/3d/buy</code> — redirects to Cart</li>
            <li><code>/3d/order</code> — place a print order</li>
            <li><code>/3d/my_orders</code> — customer order history</li>
            <li><code>/3d/queue</code> — print job queue (admin)</li>
            <li><code>/3d/queue_print</code> — mark job as printed</li>
            <li><code>/3d/queue_sync</code> — sync queue with inventory/consignment</li>
            <li><code>/3d/printers</code> — printer farm management</li>
            <li><code>/3d/admin</code> — admin dashboard</li>
            <li><code>/3d/models</code> — model library management</li>
            <li><code>/3d/model_stl_info/&lt;id&gt;</code> — geometry stats for a model</li>
            <li><code>/3d/search_deeper</code> — deeper inventory search</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>STL Upload &amp; Parser</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>File uploads handled by <code>FileManager</code>; accepts <code>.stl</code>, <code>.3mf</code>, <code>.obj</code>, <code>.gcode</code>.</li>
            <li>Built-in <code>_parse_stl</code> method reads binary STL headers, counts triangles, estimates bounding box dimensions.</li>
            <li>NaN guards prevent failures on non-STL files passed to the parser.</li>
            <li>Upload errors are surfaced in flash messages (no silent fail).</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Model Manager</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>Printing3dModel</code> Result class — stores model metadata and file path.</li>
            <li>Models link to Inventory items via foreign key, enabling stock tracking.</li>
            <li><code>show_in_shop</code> flag controls marketplace visibility.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Printer Farm</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>Printing3dPrinter</code> / <code>Printing3dPrinters</code> Result classes.</li>
            <li>Category filter on the printers page broadened to match <code>3d_printer</code>, <code>3dprinter</code>, <code>equipment</code>, and variants.</li>
            <li>Asset links corrected to <code>/Inventory/item/view</code>.</li>
            <li>Evals split per table: missing <code>inventory_equipment</code> table no longer silently kills the whole page.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Print Queue</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>Printing3dJob</code> Result class with consignment columns for queue-to-consignment integration.</li>
            <li><code>queue_sync</code> reconciles the print queue with the inventory/consignment system.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Consignment Integration</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>"Consign from 3D admin" link added to the 3D admin dashboard.</li>
            <li>Cross-site consignment with <code>source_sitename</code> selector.</li>
            <li>Consignment form line items use <code>shop_options</code> for colour/filament selectors; options stored in line notes.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Navigation</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>TopDropList3d.tt</code> — new top-nav dropdown for 3D printing.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Files Changed</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/3d.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/Printing3dJob.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/Printing3dModel.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/Printing3dPrinter.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/Printing3dPrinters.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>root/3d/</code> — admin, browse, index, model_detail, models, my_orders, order, printers, queue, queue_print, queue_sync, store templates</li>
            <li><code>root/Navigation/TopDropList3d.tt</code></li>
            <li><code>root/Inventory/consignment/new.tt</code>, <code>list.tt</code>, <code>view.tt</code>, <code>print.tt</code></li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
</div>
<div id="2026-04-28-beekeeping-hive-inspection" class="cl-entry">
<h3>Beekeeping: Hive Inspection System</h3>
&#91;% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %&#93;&#91;% PageVersion %&#93;&#91;% END %&#93;







<div class="changelog-entry">
    <header class="changelog-header">
        <h1>Beekeeping: Hive Inspection System</h1>
        <div class="changelog-meta">
            <span class="date">April 28, 2026</span>
            <span class="author">by shanta</span>
            <span class="type">New Feature</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="changelog-summary">
        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <p>The Apiary controller gained a complete hive inspection module with CRUD inspection records, inspection calendar view, printable inspection reports, and an interactive visual hive diagram. New DB Result classes support inspection details, feeding records, hive frame state, and hive/queen history.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="changelog-details">
        <h2>Inspection Routes</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>/Apiary/inspections</code> — list all inspections</li>
            <li><code>/Apiary/inspections/new</code> — new inspection form</li>
            <li><code>/Apiary/inspections/create</code> — POST to save inspection (transactional)</li>
            <li><code>/Apiary/inspections/view/&lt;id&gt;</code> — view a single inspection</li>
            <li><code>/Apiary/inspections/edit/&lt;id&gt;</code> — edit form</li>
            <li><code>/Apiary/inspections/update/&lt;id&gt;</code> — POST update (transactional)</li>
            <li><code>/Apiary/inspections/reports</code> — printable inspection reports</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Visual Hive Diagram</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>_hive_diagram.tt</code> — SVG/HTML partial that renders a visual representation of a hive's box and frame configuration.</li>
            <li>Included on inspection view and hive management pages.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Inspection Calendar</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>inspection_calendar.tt</code> — calendar grid showing inspections by date, linking to individual inspection records.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>DB Result Classes Added</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>Inspection</code> — top-level inspection record (hive, date, inspector, overall observations)</li>
            <li><code>InspectionDetail</code> — per-box/frame observations within an inspection</li>
            <li><code>InspectionFeeding</code> — feeding records linked to inspections</li>
            <li><code>HiveFrame</code> — frame state (drawn, brood, honey, pollen coverage)</li>
            <li><code>HiveAssembly</code> — hive box configuration records</li>
            <li><code>HiveConfiguration</code> / <code>HiveConfigurationHistory</code> — hive setup and changes over time</li>
            <li><code>HiveMovement</code> / <code>FrameMovement</code> — movement audit trail</li>
            <li><code>QueenEvent</code> / <code>Queen_events</code> — queen events (swarm, supersedure, re-queen)</li>
            <li><code>QueenHiveAssignment</code> / <code>Queen_hive_assignments</code> — queen-to-hive history</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>BMaster / Beekeeping Navigation</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>BMaster/apiary.tt</code> — apiary overview page updated with inspection links.</li>
            <li><code>BMaster/BMaster.tt</code> — context-aware beekeeping menu.</li>
            <li><code>Navigation/TopDropListBeekeeping.tt</code> — beekeeping top-nav dropdown.</li>
            <li>Apiary info page added; redirect loop in guest navigation fixed.</li>
            <li>Guest navigation improvements for the beekeeping area.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Configuration</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>ConfigurationBox</code> Result class — hive box configuration options.</li>
            <li><code>ConfigurationInventory</code> Result class — maps hive configuration to inventory items.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Files Changed</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Apiary.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/BMaster.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/ApiaryModel.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/Inspection.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/InspectionDetail.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/InspectionFeeding.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/HiveFrame.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/HiveAssembly.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/HiveConfiguration.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/HiveConfigurationHistory.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/HiveMovement.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/FrameMovement.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/QueenEvent.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/QueenHiveAssignment.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/ConfigurationBox.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/ConfigurationInventory.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>root/Apiary/</code> — all inspection templates + hive diagram</li>
            <li><code>root/BMaster/apiary.tt</code>, <code>BMaster.tt</code></li>
            <li><code>root/Navigation/TopDropListBeekeeping.tt</code></li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
</div>
<div id="2026-04-28-helpdesk-ticket-lifecycle" class="cl-entry">
<h3>HelpDesk Ticket Lifecycle</h3>
&#91;% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %&#93;&#91;% PageVersion %&#93;&#91;% END %&#93;







<div class="changelog-entry">
    <header class="changelog-header">
        <h1>HelpDesk: Ticket Lifecycle</h1>
        <div class="changelog-meta">
            <span class="date">April 28, 2026</span>
            <span class="author">by shanta</span>
            <span class="type">Feature Addition</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="changelog-summary">
        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <p>Implemented a complete support-ticket lifecycle in the HelpDesk controller, covering staff status management, customer reminder emails, automatic stale-ticket closure, customer-reply reopen logic, and site-admin email notifications for all key events.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="changelog-details">
        <h2>New Endpoints</h2>

        <h3>POST /HelpDesk/ticket/update_status/&lt;ticket_number&gt;</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Staff-only action to change a ticket's status (open → resolved, closed, on_hold, etc.).</li>
            <li>Accepts optional <code>resolution</code> parameter which is recorded as an audit note in TicketMessage.</li>
            <li>When status becomes <em>resolved</em> or <em>closed</em>, sends the customer an email with a public link to reopen by replying.</li>
            <li>Old and new status are logged via <code>log_with_details</code>.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>POST /HelpDesk/ticket/remind/&lt;ticket_number&gt;</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Sends a reminder email to the customer referencing the open ticket.</li>
            <li>Only available to staff; redirects non-staff with a flash error.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Auto-Close Stale Tickets</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>_auto_close_stale_tickets</code> is called on every <code>admin_tickets</code> load.</li>
            <li>Any ticket in <em>resolved</em> status that has not been updated in 14+ days is automatically moved to <em>closed</em>.</li>
            <li>A system TicketMessage is appended recording the auto-close date.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Reopen on Customer Reply</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>When a customer posts a reply (<code>ticket_reply</code>) on a <em>resolved</em> or <em>closed</em> ticket, the ticket status is automatically reset to <em>open</em>.</li>
            <li>A TicketMessage with <code>message_type = 'status_change'</code> is logged to record the reopen event.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Site-Admin Email Notifications</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>_notify_site_admins</code> helper sends email to all users with the <em>admin</em> role for the site when:
                <ul>
                    <li>A new ticket is submitted.</li>
                    <li>Any reply is posted (staff or customer).</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li>CSC site admins receive notifications across all sites; other sites only see their own tickets.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Admin Ticket Views</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>/HelpDesk/admin/tickets/open</code> — open tickets only.</li>
            <li><code>/HelpDesk/admin/tickets/closed</code> — closed tickets.</li>
            <li><code>/HelpDesk/admin/tickets/resolved</code> — resolved (awaiting auto-close).</li>
            <li><code>/HelpDesk/admin/tickets_alert</code> — alert endpoint used by Daily Plan panel.</li>
            <li>CSC admins see tickets across all sites; other site-admins see their site only.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Files Changed</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/HelpDesk.pm</code> — all new lifecycle actions</li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/SupportTicket.pm</code> — status field</li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/TicketMessage.pm</code> — message_type field</li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Util/EmailNotification.pm</code> — send helper</li>
            <li><code>root/CSC/HelpDesk/ticket_view.tt</code>, <code>ticket_status.tt</code>, <code>admin_tickets.tt</code>, <code>admin.tt</code></li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
</div>
<div id="2026-04-28-inventory-shop-hosting-membership" class="cl-entry">
<h3>Inventory, Shop, Hosting, Membership &amp;amp; Point System</h3>
&#91;% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %&#93;&#91;% PageVersion %&#93;&#91;% END %&#93;







<div class="changelog-entry">
    <header class="changelog-header">
        <h1>Inventory, Shop, Hosting, Membership &amp; Point System</h1>
        <div class="changelog-meta">
            <span class="date">April 28, 2026</span>
            <span class="author">by shanta</span>
            <span class="type">Major Feature Release</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="changelog-summary">
        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <p>A large multi-system release merging the <code>inventory-system-104a</code> branch into main. Covers a complete inventory management system (items, BOM, stock, labels, consignment), a shop/marketplace, a full hosting management system with cost configuration, a membership plan-details popup, and a points/credit ledger with commission hooks and an admin log-credits UI.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="changelog-details">
        <h2>Inventory System</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Items: add, edit, list with <code>datalist</code> category suggestions (3d_printer, filament, equipment, supplies, etc.).</li>
            <li><code>unit_price</code> used throughout — <code>selling_price</code> column does not exist in DB and was removed.</li>
            <li>BOM (Bill of Materials): list and view templates.</li>
            <li>Stock levels view: <code>/Inventory/stock/levels</code>.</li>
            <li>Print templates: label, multi-label, BOM print, stock report.</li>
            <li>Consignment: new, view, list, print. Cross-site consignment with <code>source_sitename</code> selector. Line items use <code>script</code>-element cloning for maximum browser compatibility.</li>
            <li>Supplier invoice: <code>post_supplier_invoice</code> stock_level find-or-create bug fixed.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Shop &amp; Marketplace</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>New <code>Shop</code> controller and templates for a site-hosted shop/marketplace.</li>
            <li>Cart integration.</li>
            <li>COA (Chart of Accounts) integration.</li>
            <li>Items flagged <code>show_in_shop</code> appear in the shop listing.</li>
            <li>3D store (<code>/3d/store</code>) redirects to <code>/shop</code>; <code>/3d/buy</code> goes to Cart.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Hosting Management</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>/hosted</code> — hosted dashboard for customers.</li>
            <li><code>/accounts</code> — admin account management.</li>
            <li><code>/hosting/activate</code> — activate a hosting account.</li>
            <li><code>/hosting/cost</code> — admin UI for hosting cost configuration.</li>
            <li><code>/hosting/setup</code> — creates hosting tables and seeds config via app API (one-time setup endpoint).</li>
            <li><code>/apply</code> redirects to <code>/hosting_signup</code>.</li>
            <li>Hosting admin access fixed: redirects to login (not home) when unauthenticated.</li>
            <li><code>HostingCostConfig</code> Result class added.</li>
            <li><code>membership/admin/hosting_accounts.tt</code> added to membership admin area.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Membership</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>PlanDetails.tt</code> now includes a signup popup modal — users can initiate signup from the plan details page without leaving it.</li>
            <li><code>site_name</code> passed into the <code>plan_details</code> action for correct plan scoping.</li>
            <li><code>membership/hosting_signup.tt</code> updated.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Point System (<code>Comserv::Util::PointSystem</code>)</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Full credit/debit ledger with <code>SitePointAccount</code> Result class.</li>
            <li>Methods: <code>balance</code>, <code>ensure_account</code>, <code>apply_joining_bonus</code>, <code>apply_plan_bonus</code>, <code>credit</code>, <code>debit</code>, <code>transfer</code>, <code>record_payment</code>, <code>credit_site_account</code>, <code>apply_hosting_commission</code>.</li>
            <li><code>Todo.pm award_points</code> — awards points when a todo is completed.</li>
            <li>Commission hooks fire on hosting activation/renewal.</li>
            <li><code>PointRule</code> Result class with <code>resolve_rate()</code> helper — looks up the applicable rate for a role (founder royalty config).</li>
            <li>Admin log-credits UI at <code>/admin/Logging/LogCredits</code>.</li>
            <li>Batch back-credit script for retroactive point awards.</li>
            <li><code>FounderRoyaltyConfig</code> Result class added.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Files Changed (key)</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Inventory.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Hosting.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Membership.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Todo.pm</code> — award_points</li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Util/PointSystem.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/InventoryItem.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/SitePointAccount.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/FounderRoyaltyConfig.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/HostingCostConfig.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>root/Inventory/</code> — all item, BOM, stock, consignment, print templates</li>
            <li><code>root/hosting/</code> — admin_accounts, cost_config, hosted_dashboard, setup</li>
            <li><code>root/membership/</code> — PlanDetails, hosting_signup, Index, admin/hosting_accounts</li>
            <li><code>root/admin/Logging/LogCredits.tt</code></li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
</div>
<div id="2026-04-28-planning-system-daily-plan" class="cl-entry">
<h3>Planning System: Daily Plan Enhancements</h3>
&#91;% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %&#93;&#91;% PageVersion %&#93;&#91;% END %&#93;







<div class="changelog-entry">
    <header class="changelog-header">
        <h1>Planning System: Daily Plan Enhancements</h1>
        <div class="changelog-meta">
            <span class="date">April 28, 2026</span>
            <span class="author">by shanta</span>
            <span class="type">Feature Enhancement</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="changelog-summary">
        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <p>Major overhaul of the Daily Plan interface (<code>/planning/daily</code>): added an AI-assisted Start Day action, an Audit Todos panel, a HelpDesk open-tickets panel, morning notes that preserve auto-generated preamble, an action bar below the tab toolbar, and a live View Log button.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="changelog-details">
        <h2>Start Day — AI-Assisted Audit</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>POST <code>/planning/daily</code> with <code>action=start_day</code> triggers an AI audit of all open/critical todos.</li>
            <li>The controller groups blocking todos by controller/subroutine, deduplicates, and passes a structured map to the AI planning agent.</li>
            <li>AI response is written into the daily log as a "Morning Summary" entry.</li>
            <li>HelpDesk open-ticket count is fetched via <code>/HelpDesk/admin/tickets_alert</code> and included in the start-day briefing.</li>
            <li><code>record_id</code> is correctly passed through the end action to avoid FK violation on log save.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Daily Plan Panels (always visible)</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Audit Todos panel</strong> — collapsible, shows any open P1/P2/P3 todos (not filtered to today only). WARN-level errors are included at P3 priority. CRITICAL/ERROR = P1.</li>
            <li><strong>HelpDesk panel</strong> — collapsible, shows open support tickets. CSC admins see all sites; other site admins see their own.</li>
            <li><strong>Priorities panel</strong> — existing panel retained.</li>
            <li>All three panels are always rendered (with empty-state messages) so the page layout is consistent.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Morning Notes</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>The morning notes section now shows <em>only</em> the user-editable notes textarea (not the full auto-generated preamble).</li>
            <li>On save, the auto-generated preamble from the existing log entry is preserved and prepended before the user's notes.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Action Bar &amp; Toolbar</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Action bar is rendered below the tab row (not inside a tab) so it's always visible.</li>
            <li><strong>Start Day button</strong> replaces the old "Good Morning" hardcoded link.</li>
            <li><strong>View Log / Today's Log button</strong> toggles the log panel; becomes active when the log is open.</li>
            <li>Start Day auto-opens the log panel on success.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Log Entry Fixes</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Fixed <code>open_log_entry</code>: now uses <code>record_id</code> not <code>id</code> in the DB search.</li>
            <li>Username search corrected in the morning summary query.</li>
            <li>SystemLog column names corrected: <code>file</code> and <code>line</code> (not <code>filename</code>/<code>line_number</code>).</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Plan Management</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Plan edit form (<code>GET/POST /admin/plan/edit_form</code>) added with a matching <code>edit.tt</code> template.</li>
            <li>Plan view now includes a form to link the plan to a project via a dropdown of available projects.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Proxy Debug Message Removed</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>Root.pm site_setup</code> no longer outputs proxy debug_msg to every page response.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Files Changed</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Planning.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Admin/PlanManagement.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Root.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>root/admin/planning/DailyPlan.tt</code></li>
            <li><code>root/admin/plan/edit.tt</code>, <code>root/admin/plan/view.tt</code></li>
            <li><code>root/log/details.tt</code></li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
</div>
<div id="2026-04-28-todo-priority-system" class="cl-entry">
<h3>Todo Priority System &amp;amp; Enhancements</h3>
&#91;% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %&#93;&#91;% PageVersion %&#93;&#91;% END %&#93;







<div class="changelog-entry">
    <header class="changelog-header">
        <h1>Todo Priority System &amp; Enhancements</h1>
        <div class="changelog-meta">
            <span class="date">April 28, 2026</span>
            <span class="author">by shanta</span>
            <span class="type">Enhancement</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="changelog-summary">
        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <p>Priority labels are now a single source of truth in <code>Comserv::Util::Priority</code>. The todo details form gained an editable <code>accumulative_time</code> field, a labeled priority dropdown, and a 12-hour time selector. Status handling was normalized in Perl (not TT2) to eliminate string/numeric comparison bugs. Auto-error todo creation now correctly matches the controller name to a project.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="changelog-details">
        <h2>Comserv::Util::Priority — Single Source of Truth</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>New module at <code>lib/Comserv/Util/Priority.pm</code> exports <code>priority_options()</code>.</li>
            <li>Returns a hashref mapping numeric priority (1–10) to self-explanatory label strings:
                <ul>
                    <li>1 — P1: Critical — system/site broken, stop everything</li>
                    <li>2 — P2: Urgent — blocking key work, must resolve today</li>
                    <li>3 — P3: High — important, complete this sprint</li>
                    <li>4 — P4: Above Normal — scheduled soon, next sprint</li>
                    <li>5 — P5: Medium — standard backlog item</li>
                    <li>6 — P6: Normal — background work, no deadline pressure</li>
                    <li>7 — P7: Low — address when capacity allows</li>
                    <li>8 — P8: Minor — nice to have, no immediate impact</li>
                    <li>9 — P9: Minimal — someday/maybe</li>
                    <li>10 — P10: Optional — wishlist only</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li>All controllers and templates that previously had inline priority arrays now call <code>priority_options()</code>.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Todo Details Form Enhancements</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Accumulative time field</strong> — editable text input in <code>details.tt</code> edit form, persisted in the <code>accumulative_time</code> column.</li>
            <li><strong>Priority dropdown</strong> — now shows self-explanatory labels (e.g. "P1: Critical — system/site broken") instead of bare numbers. Sorted numerically.</li>
            <li><strong>12-hour time selector</strong> — time fields use a 12-hour AM/PM selector for better usability.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Status Normalization</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>normalize_status</code> in the controller now handles <code>In-Process</code>, <code>inprocess</code>, and mixed-case variants, mapping them to <code>In Process</code>.</li>
            <li>Status is normalized in Perl before being stored/displayed — TT2 templates use <code>current_status</code> (already a clean string) and the <code>eq</code> operator for string comparison, not <code>==</code>.</li>
            <li>A <code>normalize_todo_status.pl</code> cleanup script is provided to retroactively fix inconsistent status values in the DB.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Auto-Error Todo Creation</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>When an application error auto-creates a todo, the controller name is now matched against the project list to assign the todo to the correct project.</li>
            <li>Fixes cases where error todos landed in the wrong project bucket.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Other Fixes</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Todo save now preserves all existing fields when only some fields are submitted (no accidental field erasure).</li>
            <li>Todo modify redirects correctly after save.</li>
            <li>Todo edit FK violation on the planning system fixed by passing correct <code>record_id</code>.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Files Changed</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Util/Priority.pm</code> — new module</li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Todo.pm</code></li>
            <li><code>root/todo/details.tt</code></li>
            <li><code>root/todo/edit.tt</code></li>
            <li><code>root/todo/priority_select.tt</code></li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
</div>
<div id="2026-08-10-ai-model-catalog-single-source" class="cl-entry">
<h3>AI Model Catalog &amp;mdash; Single Source of Truth &amp;amp; Chat Widget Repair</h3>
&#91;% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %&#93;&#91;% PageVersion %&#93;&#91;% END %&#93;







<div class="changelog-entry">
    <header class="changelog-header">
        <h1>AI Model Catalog &mdash; Single Source of Truth &amp; Chat Widget Repair</h1>
        <div class="changelog-meta">
            <span class="date">August 10, 2026</span>
            <span class="author">by shanta</span>
            <span class="type">Bug Fix / Refactor</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="changelog-summary">
        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <p>
            Repaired the AI chat regression that emptied the &ldquo;Chat with AI&rdquo; widget
            and removed the model list from every page, then consolidated model
            selection into one server-side source of truth,
            <code>Comserv::Util::ModelCatalog</code>. Model dropdowns are now
            server-rendered from a single partial, filtered to real chat models,
            cost-labelled, and default to a free model instead of silently loading
            the workstation GPU.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="changelog-details">
        <h2>Root causes fixed</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Lowercase <code>Process</code> in Template Toolkit.</strong> All three
                call sites invoked the shared dropdown partial with a lowercase
                <code>Process</code>. TT directives are UPPERCASE; the lowercase form
                parses as an undefined variable and renders nothing, leaving an empty
                <code>&lt;select&gt;</code> on <code>/ai</code>, <code>/ai2</code> and the
                floating widget.</li>
            <li><strong>Popup bypassed the shared loader.</strong> <code>/ai/widget</code> is
                rendered by <code>widget.tt</code> through a standalone
                <code>Template-&gt;new</code> with no Catalyst context, so it never received
                the catalog stash or the cache-buster; it served a frozen
                <code>?v=1</code> and an empty widget.</li>
            <li><strong>Malformed partial.</strong> <code>ai/model_select.tt</code> leaked its own
                comment text into the page and its grouping loop produced no options.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>New: Comserv::Util::ModelCatalog</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Single source of truth for the AI model list across every surface:
                floating widget, <code>/ai/widget</code> popup, <code>/ai</code>,
                <code>/ai2</code>, the AI2 editor and the git dashboard.</li>
            <li>Built once per process from the v2 Router
                (<code>Model::AI2-&gt;get_available_models</code>) &mdash; the same source
                <code>/ai2/providers</code> uses &mdash; and cached with a 600&nbsp;second TTL.</li>
            <li><code>prime()</code> lets <code>Controller::AI2::providers</code> populate the
                cache from a catalog it already built, avoiding a second provider
                round-trip.</li>
            <li>Failure is non-destructive: a failed rebuild keeps the last good cache
                and retries in 30&nbsp;seconds rather than blanking the dropdown.</li>
            <li>Strips Router sentinels (<code>ollama_empty</code>,
                <code>ollama_unreachable</code>, <code>*_unconfigured</code>) so status markers
                are never offered as selectable models.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Cost-aware presentation</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Each entry carries <code>free</code>, <code>local</code> and <code>paid</code> flags.</li>
            <li>Free models sort first inside their provider group and are labelled
                &ldquo;&mdash;&nbsp;free&rdquo;; Ollama models are labelled &ldquo;&mdash;&nbsp;local&rdquo;.</li>
            <li>Non-chat families (embeddings, rerankers, image, audio, video,
                moderation) are filtered out: 414 catalog entries render as 397 options.</li>
            <li><code>default_for()</code> pre-selects a free OpenRouter model for guests and
                ordinary members, and the pinned coding model for privileged users on a
                coding surface. Previously the browser selected the first option
                alphabetically, which silently routed every guest to a local Ollama
                model and loaded the already-saturated workstation GPU.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Follow-up fix &mdash; wrong provider used and mislabelled</h2>
        <p>
            After the catalog repair, selecting a free OpenRouter model still produced
            an answer labelled &ldquo;Ollama (Local): tencent/hy3&rdquo;. Four separate
            defects, all fixed:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Auto-tiering hijacked external selections.</strong>
                <code>autoSelectProvider()</code> only ever returns local Ollama tiers
                (<code>state.modelTiers</code> contains nothing else). Because the
                server-rendered default does not set <code>userModelOverride</code>,
                auto-tiering ran and replaced the chosen OpenRouter model with an Ollama
                one. It now returns the current selection unchanged whenever that
                selection is not Ollama.</li>
            <li><strong>Hardcoded <code>'ollama'</code> default.</strong>
                <code>state.selectedProvider</code> was initialised to
                <code>'ollama'</code> and never synced from the server-rendered
                <code>&lt;select&gt;</code>, so the request went local while the dropdown
                displayed something else. It now starts empty and
                <code>mountProviderSelect()</code> adopts the server default.</li>
            <li><strong>Labels assumed &ldquo;not Grok therefore Ollama&rdquo;.</strong> Both
                the change handler and the response handler built the status string that
                way, so every OpenRouter model was announced as Ollama. Replaced with a
                shared <code>describeModel()</code> helper in
                <code>ai-chat/model-select.js</code> that derives the provider from the
                <code>provider|model</code> value.</li>
            <li><strong>Popup never loaded the shared module.</strong>
                <code>widget.tt</code> omitted <code>ai-chat/model-select.js</code>, so
                <code>describeModel()</code> fell back to a crude inline version and the
                backend's generic bucket name <code>external</code> leaked into the UI.
                The script is now included, and <code>describeModel()</code> maps
                <code>external</code> with a slash-bearing slug to OpenRouter.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Verified live in the popup: status now reads
            &ldquo;OpenRouter: nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-30b-a3b:free&rdquo; with a real
            model response and no console errors.
        </p>

        <h2>Files changed</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Util/ModelCatalog.pm</code> &mdash; new</li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Root.pm</code> &mdash; stash catalog + default from the util</li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/AI.pm</code> &mdash; widget passes catalog, default and <code>css_v</code> explicitly</li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/AI2.pm</code> &mdash; primes the shared cache</li>
            <li><code>root/ai/model_select.tt</code> &mdash; rewritten shared partial</li>
            <li><code>root/ai/widget.tt</code> &mdash; catalog global, server-rendered select, dynamic cache-buster</li>
            <li><code>root/js_load.tt</code>, <code>root/ai/index.tt</code>, <code>root/ai2/index.tt</code> &mdash; <code>PROCESS</code> fix</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Follow-up plan</h2>
        <p>
            Remaining work &mdash; per-model pricing, premium filtering, page and role
            scoped shortlists, usage telemetry, and the standing v2-migration and
            documentation-sync rules &mdash; is tracked in
            <a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/Documentation/AIModelPresentationPlan') %&#93;">AI Model Presentation &amp; Selection</a>
            (project 252, phases 253&ndash;257, todos 2020&ndash;2035).
        </p>
    </section>
</div>
</div>
<div id="2026-08-10-ai2-providers-hashref-guard" class="cl-entry">
<h3>AI2 Providers &amp;mdash; guard against malformed catalog elements</h3>
&#91;% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %&#93;&#91;% PageVersion %&#93;&#91;% END %&#93;







<div class="changelog-entry">
    <header class="changelog-header">
        <h1>AI2 Providers &mdash; guard against malformed catalog elements</h1>
        <div class="changelog-meta">
            <span class="date">August 10, 2026</span>
            <span class="author">by shanta</span>
            <span class="type">Bug Fix</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="changelog-summary">
        <p>
            An unauthenticated (guest-tier) request to <code>/ai2/providers</code> at bmaster
            returned the <strong>correct free model list</strong> yet also raised
            <em>&ldquo;Not a HASH reference at Controller/AI2.pm line 76&rdquo;</em>, which
            spawned an error-audit todo. The grouping loop dereferenced
            <code>$m-&gt;{provider}</code> on every element of the catalog; one element was
            not a hashref &mdash; an upstream provider JSON anomaly (Ollama
            <code>/api/tags</code> or OpenRouter <code>/v1/models</code> occasionally returns a
            non-object entry).
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="changelog-details">
        <h2>Fix</h2>
        <p>Two layers now reject non-hash elements instead of dying:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/AI2.pm::providers</code> &mdash; the per-element
                loop skips any entry whose <code>ref</code> is not <code>HASH</code>, logging an
                <code>ai2_providers</code> warning that records the offending element's shape
                (scalar string / array / other ref / undef).</li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/AI2/Router.pm::get_available_models</code> &mdash;
                sanitizes the assembled catalog immediately before the role filter, dropping any
                non-hashref element and logging a <code>get_available_models</code> warning with
                the element's shape. Because <code>get_available_models</code> is the single
                source of truth, the bad element is already gone before the chat widget,
                <code>/ai</code>, <code>/ai2</code> and the git dashboard consume it.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Why defensive rather than a one-line type check</h2>
        <p>
            The catalog is built entirely from upstream provider JSON, so a malformed entry is an
            <em>environment</em> fault, not a code fault we can reproduce by inspection. Dropping
            the bad entry keeps the endpoint healthy for every other user, and the accompanying
            warning captures the exact payload on the next occurrence so the responsible provider
            API can be fixed at the boundary if it recurs. The guest request that triggered this
            had already returned the right data &mdash; the 500 was purely the loop choking on one
            stray element.
        </p>

        <h2>Verified</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>perl -c</code> clean on <code>Controller/AI2.pm</code> and
                <code>Model/AI2/Router.pm</code>.</li>
            <li>The endpoint now degrades gracefully: a malformed entry is dropped, not fatal.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Files changed</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/AI2.pm</code> &mdash; skip + log non-hash elements in <code>providers</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/AI2/Router.pm</code> &mdash; sanitize catalog before role filter in <code>get_available_models</code></li>
            <li><code>root/Documentation/changelog/2026-08-10-ai2-providers-hashref-guard.tt</code> &mdash; this entry</li>
            <li><code>root/Documentation/changelog/CHANGELOG.tt</code> &mdash; [Unreleased] bullet cross-linked here</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Related</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/Documentation/changelog/2026-08-10-ai-model-catalog-single-source') %&#93;">AI Model Catalog &mdash; Single Source of Truth</a></li>
            <li><a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/Documentation/changelog/2026-08-10-model-role-filter') %&#93;">AI model list &mdash; role-based visibility</a></li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
</div>
<div id="2026-08-10-focustune-default-model" class="cl-entry">
<h3>AI Focus-Tune — Use catalog default model, not hardcoded phi4:14b</h3>
&#91;% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %&#93;&#91;% PageVersion %&#93;&#91;% END %&#93;







<div class="changelog-entry">
    <header class="changelog-header">
        <h1>AI Focus-Tune default model — de-hardcoded</h1>
        <div class="changelog-meta">
            <span class="date">August 10, 2026</span>
            <span class="author">by shanta</span>
            <span class="type">Bug fix / daily-plan AI Focus-Tune</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="changelog-summary">
        <p>
            The daily-plan <strong>AI Focus-Tune</strong> (the 🤖 AI: Tune / ⚖ Compare
            buttons on Today&rsquo;s Focus Queue &mdash; &ldquo;ask AI to check the accuracy of
            the top 20&rdquo;) hardcoded <code>phi4:14b</code> (a localhost Ollama model) as
            its default in three client-side spots and as the server fallback. On a box where
            Ollama is unreachable (or where the user should be on a free/paid OpenRouter model),
            the tune would silently run on the wrong model. The default is now derived from the
            <strong>same shared catalog</strong> every other AI surface uses.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="changelog-details">
        <h2>What changed</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>Controller::Api::_focus_default_model($c)</code> (new) returns
                <code>ModelCatalog-&gt;default_for(page =&gt; 'chat')</code> &mdash; the
                free OpenRouter default for guests/members, or the pinned coding model for
                privileged users &mdash; in <code>provider|model</code> form. Falls back to the
                first catalog entry, then to a hard safe default only if the catalog is empty.</li>
            <li><code>GET /api/focus/models</code> now returns a <code>default</code> field
                (the catalog default) alongside <code>models</code>.</li>
            <li><code>api_focus_top5</code> uses the catalog default instead of the literal
                <code>phi4:14b</code> when no model is explicitly selected.</li>
            <li><code>daily-plan-utils.js</code>: the three <code>phi4:14b</code> literals
                (the <code>_aiTuneTargets</code> fallback, the model-popup init, and the
                <code>.catch</code> fallback) now read <code>_aiTuneDefault</code>, populated
                from the server&rsquo;s <code>default</code> field. No client-side model
                hardcode remains.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Verified</h2>
        <p>
            Live <code>GET /api/focus/models</code> returns
            <code>default: openrouter|nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-30b-a3b:free</code> and the model
            picker now pre-selects that default. <code>perl -c</code> on Api.pm and
            <code>node --check</code> on daily-plan-utils.js both pass.
        </p>

        <h2>Files changed</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Api.pm</code> &mdash; add <code>_focus_default_model</code>; use it in <code>api_focus_models</code> + <code>api_focus_top5</code></li>
            <li><code>root/static/js/planning/daily-plan-utils.js</code> &mdash; drive default from server <code>default</code> field, remove <code>phi4:14b</code> literals</li>
            <li><code>root/Documentation/changelog/2026-08-10-focustune-default-model.tt</code> &mdash; this entry</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
</div>
<div id="2026-08-10-focustune-dehardcode" class="cl-entry">
<h3>AI Focus-Tune — De-hardcode top-N and finish removing phi4:14b</h3>
&#91;% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %&#93;&#91;% PageVersion %&#93;&#91;% END %&#93;







<div class="changelog-entry">
    <header class="changelog-header">
        <h1>AI Focus-Tune — de-hardcode top-N + finish phi4:14b removal</h1>
        <div class="changelog-meta">
            <span class="date">August 10, 2026</span>
            <span class="author">by shanta</span>
            <span class="type">Bug fix / daily-plan AI Focus-Tune</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="changelog-summary">
        <p>
            The daily-plan &ldquo;ask AI to check the accuracy of the top 20&rdquo; (AI
            Focus-Tune) still had hardcoded literals: the candidate/prompt/comparison sizes
            (<code>50</code> / <code>25</code> / <code>19</code>) were bare magic numbers in
            <code>FocusTune.pm</code>, and <code>phi4:14b</code> remained as the client-side
            fallback in <code>daily-plan-utils.js</code>. Both are now de-hardcoded.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="changelog-details">
        <h2>What changed</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>FocusTune.pm</code> &mdash; added named constants
                <code>CANDIDATE_CAP =&gt; 50</code>, <code>PROMPT_CAP =&gt; 25</code>,
                <code>COMPARE_TOP =&gt; 20</code>. The candidate <code>splice</code>, the prompt
                cap, and the coded-vs-AI &ldquo;top 20&rdquo; diff slices all use these instead
                of <code>50</code> / <code>25</code> / <code>19</code>. One place to tune.</li>
            <li><code>daily-plan-utils.js</code> &mdash; the three <code>phi4:14b</code> literals
                are gone. The default is now seeded from
                <code>window.ComservConfig.aiFocusDefault</code> (set by the daily page from the
                shared catalog default) and falls back to the server&rsquo;s
                <code>/api/focus/models</code> <code>default</code> field; only a last-resort
                free-OpenRouter slug remains as an absolute safety net (never a localhost Ollama).</li>
            <li><code>_today_work_tab.tt</code> &mdash; emits
                <code>window.ComservConfig.aiFocusDefault</code> from
                <code>ai_default_model</code> so the picker is seeded before any
                <code>/api/focus/models</code> fetch.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Verified</h2>
        <p>
            <code>grep -c phi4:14b</code> on <code>daily-plan-utils.js</code> = 0.
            <code>perl -c</code> on Router.pm / FocusTune.pm / ModelCatalog.pm and
            <code>node --check</code> on daily-plan-utils.js all pass. The Role filter from the
            prior change remains active at the Router level (guest widget still shows 19
            free/Ollama models).
        </p>

        <h2>Files changed</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/AI2/FocusTune.pm</code> &mdash; named top-N constants</li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/AI2/Router.pm</code> &mdash; role filter at get_available_models (see model-role-filter changelog)</li>
            <li><code>root/static/js/planning/daily-plan-utils.js</code> &mdash; seed default from catalog, remove phi4:14b</li>
            <li><code>root/admin/planning/_today_work_tab.tt</code> &mdash; emit aiFocusDefault global</li>
            <li><code>root/Documentation/changelog/2026-08-10-focustune-dehardcode.tt</code> &mdash; this entry</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
</div>
<div id="2026-08-10-infra-ha-load-balancing-session-state" class="cl-entry">
<h3>INFRA-HA &amp;mdash; Load balancing reality, and two state blockers found in the code</h3>
&#91;% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %&#93;&#91;% PageVersion %&#93;&#91;% END %&#93;







<div class="changelog-entry">
    <header class="changelog-header">
        <h1>INFRA-HA &mdash; Load balancing reality, and two state blockers</h1>
        <div class="changelog-meta">
            <span class="date">August 10, 2026</span>
            <span class="author">by shanta</span>
            <span class="type">Planning / INFRA-HA (#202) + AUTH-EVO (#243)</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="changelog-summary">
        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <p>
            Two questions were put to the
            <a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/Documentation/K3S_APP_HA_PLAN') %&#93;">Availability &amp;
            Load Balancing Master Plan</a>: does Kubernetes actually pick the best container
            per request, and if consecutive calls land on different containers, does session
            and temp-file storage have to change? Answering the second question required
            reading the code, which surfaced <strong>two blockers the plan did not know
            about</strong>. Documentation and todos only &mdash; <strong>no code or
            infrastructure was changed</strong>.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="changelog-details">
        <h2>&sect;3h &mdash; what k8s load balancing does, stated precisely</h2>
        <p>
            An earlier verbal answer in this workstream overstated the limitation by saying
            Kubernetes &ldquo;does not load balance&rdquo;. Corrected and recorded: it does.
            kube-proxy spreads connections across all Ready pods, readiness probes pull broken
            pods from rotation, resource requests and anti-affinity make placement
            capacity-aware, and HPA scales out under load.
        </p>
        <p>
            The single thing not enabled by default is <em>per-request least-connection
            selection</em> &mdash; the default is round-robin, which does not measure backend
            CPU or latency. That is one ingress configuration line (NGINX
            <code>least_conn</code>), not a missing capability.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>Deliberately deferred.</strong> This is an availability plan. The
            2026-08-07 outage was a container that did not exist for 100 minutes, not a
            container that was slow. Readiness probes plus <code>replicas=2</code> close that
            outage class entirely; least-request routing addresses a throughput problem the
            estate does not have. &sect;3h records the revisit trigger: enable it if E.4
            (testing under load, AI workload saturating a node) shows uneven latency.
        </p>
        <p>
            &sect;3h also clarifies that the host load figures in &sect;3d are
            <em>placement</em> evidence for a one-time human decision, not runtime inputs.
            Nothing re-reads them per request, and a 1-minute-decayed load average would be
            the wrong signal for routing anyway.
        </p>

        <h2>BLOCKER 1 &mdash; the session store is a test store (&sect;6a)</h2>
        <p>
            <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv.pm</code> line 22 loads
            <code>Session::Store::Dummy</code>, whose own documentation reads
            <em>&ldquo;Doesn't really store sessions - useful for tests.&rdquo;</em> It holds
            session data in a per-process hash in memory.
        </p>
        <p>
            This is worse than &sect;6's original &ldquo;node-local sessions&rdquo; wording:
            sessions are <strong>process-local</strong>. Two replicas would not share a login
            for one user, so every round-robin hop is a potential logout. It also means
            <strong>sessions do not survive a container restart today</strong>, on the current
            single container &mdash; testable now, independent of any HA work.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>The fix is already staged and was never switched on.</strong> The
            <code>Plugin::Session</code> config directly beneath the plugin list fully
            specifies a database store (<code>dbic_class =&gt; 'DBEncy::Session'</code>,
            <code>expires_column</code>, <code>id_column</code>, <code>data_column</code>),
            <code>Result/Session.pm</code> exists mapping the <code>sessions</code> table, and
            <code>Catalyst::Plugin::Session::Store::DBIC</code> v0.14 is installed on the host.
            A comment at line 218 claims the store is &ldquo;properly configured&rdquo;; it is
            not, and that comment should go with the fix.
        </p>
        <p>
            A second defect sits in the same area: the cookie name derives from the port
            (<code>comserv_session_$port</code>), so the 5000/3000/4000 instances on .199 issue
            differently named cookies and cannot see each other's sessions even with a shared
            store. The two call sites also disagree on the fallback default (3001 vs 4001).
            Balanced replicas must pin <code>COMSERV_SESSION_COOKIE</code> explicitly.
        </p>
        <p>
            Per &sect;11 this plan states the requirement and does not implement it. Raised as
            AUTH-R2 evidence on
            <a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/project/details') %&#93;?project_id=243">#243 (AUTH-EVO)</a>,
            todo <a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %&#93;?record_id=2046">#2046</a>.
            Switching a session store logs out every active user, so it needs a scheduled
            window.
        </p>

        <h2>BLOCKER 2 &mdash; pod-local /tmp holding cross-request state (&sect;6b)</h2>
        <p>
            <strong>Uploads are already safe.</strong> They go through
            <code>$c-&gt;path_to('root','uploads',...)</code> and the NFS mount
            (<code>NFS_HOST_PATH</code> &rarr; <code>/data/nfs</code>, present in both compose
            services). Mount the same NFS into both pods and a file uploaded via pod A is
            visible from pod B.
        </p>
        <p>
            The exposure is <code>/tmp</code> files that a <em>later</em> request reads back.
            A grep of the controllers found four:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>HIGH</strong> &mdash; <code>/tmp/whisper_job_${job_id}.status</code> and
                <code>_result.json</code> (AI.pm ~12293&ndash;12332): submit-then-poll, where the
                poll lands on the other pod and the job appears lost.</li>
            <li><strong>HIGH</strong> &mdash; <code>/tmp/comserv_chat_progress_${session_id}</code>
                (AI.pm ~8200, 8233): same failure for chat progress.</li>
            <li><strong>MEDIUM</strong> &mdash; <code>/tmp/comserv_security_scan.{txt,json}</code>
                (Admin.pm ~2828&ndash;3042): scan writes on one pod, results page reads the other.</li>
            <li><strong>MEDIUM</strong> &mdash; <code>/tmp/comserv_deploy_4000.pid</code>
                (Planning.pm ~1702): a PID file is meaningless across pods.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            <code>File::Temp</code> with <code>UNLINK =&gt; 1</code> (AI.pm ~646) is
            <strong>fine as-is</strong> &mdash; written and consumed inside one request. That is
            the dividing rule now recorded in the plan: scratch within a request may stay in
            pod-local <code>/tmp</code>; anything read back later is shared state.
        </p>
        <p>
            Tracked as todo
            <a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %&#93;?record_id=2047">#2047</a>, blocking
            Phase C. This is independent of the session fix &mdash; sharing sessions does not
            help a poll looking for a file on the wrong pod's disk.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="changelog-details">
        <h2>Why this matters beyond HA</h2>
        <p>
            Both findings are live defects, not just future obstacles. Sessions already fail to
            survive a container restart, and the <code>/tmp</code> job-status pattern already
            breaks if the background worker and the polling endpoint are ever separated. HA
            work surfaced them; it did not cause them.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="changelog-related">
        <h2>Related</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/Documentation/K3S_APP_HA_PLAN') %&#93;">Availability &amp; Load Balancing Master Plan</a> &mdash; v1.12 (&sect;3h, &sect;3i, &sect;6a, &sect;6b)</li>
            <li><a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/Documentation/2026-08-10-infra-ha-phase-a-registry-decomposition') %&#93;">Changelog: Phase A registry decomposition</a> &mdash; earlier entry, same day</li>
            <li><a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/project/details') %&#93;?project_id=202">Project #202 (INFRA-HA)</a> &mdash; todo #2047</li>
            <li><a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/project/details') %&#93;?project_id=243">Project #243 (AUTH-EVO)</a> &mdash; todo #2046, AUTH-R2 evidence</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
</div>
<div id="2026-08-10-infra-ha-phase-a-registry-decomposition" class="cl-entry">
<h3>INFRA-HA Phase A &amp;mdash; Registry decomposed, role evaluated, port conflict resolved</h3>
&#91;% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %&#93;&#91;% PageVersion %&#93;&#91;% END %&#93;







<div class="changelog-entry">
    <header class="changelog-header">
        <h1>INFRA-HA Phase A &mdash; Registry decomposition and role evaluation</h1>
        <div class="changelog-meta">
            <span class="date">August 10, 2026</span>
            <span class="author">by shanta</span>
            <span class="type">Planning / INFRA-HA (#202, sub-project #244)</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="changelog-summary">
        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <p>
            Phase A of the
            <a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/Documentation/K3S_APP_HA_PLAN') %&#93;">Availability &amp;
            Load Balancing Master Plan</a> was tracked by a single gate todo
            (<a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %&#93;?record_id=1905">#1905</a>) whose
            underlying work items had never been created &mdash; sub-project
            <a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/project/details') %&#93;?project_id=244">#244</a> was empty.
            The eight A.0&ndash;A.7 items described in the plan text now exist as real todos
            (<strong>2037&ndash;2044</strong>), the mandatory A.0 role evaluation has been
            answered from fresh measurements, and a port conflict that would have blocked
            execution was found and resolved on paper before any container was started.
            <strong>No infrastructure was changed</strong>; this entry is planning and
            documentation only.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="changelog-details">
        <h2>A.0 ROLE EVAL &mdash; re-measured, and the hosts had swapped</h2>
        <p>
            The plan mandates that every phase evaluates its host on measured evidence and
            explicitly warns &ldquo;do NOT default to .199&rdquo;. Re-measuring on 2026-08-10
            produced a materially different picture from the 2026-08-07 figures recorded in
            &sect;3d:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>.199 workstation:</strong> load 1.80 / 8 cores, 22 GB RAM available,
                <strong>80 GB disk free</strong> &mdash; previously recorded as saturated at
                8.10 / 8 with 0 GB RAM free.</li>
            <li><strong>.126 production1:</strong> load <strong>8.89 / 2 cores</strong>,
                <strong>3.2 GB disk free</strong> &mdash; previously recorded as idle at 0.06.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            The CPU load profiles inverted within three days, which is itself the lesson: a
            load reading is perishable evidence and must be re-taken per phase rather than
            reused. The figure that did <em>not</em> move is .126's disk (3.5 GB &rarr; 3.2 GB
            free). <strong>Decision: the registry goes on .199</strong>, on disk headroom
            &mdash; 80 GB against 3.2 GB. .126 is disqualified on disk alone regardless of
            load. This lands on the same host the earlier retracted draft assumed, but by a
            valid route; the coincidence does not revalidate the old &ldquo;most powerful
            machine&rdquo; reasoning, and the decision is explicitly not transferable to the
            Phase B control-plane role.
        </p>

        <h2>Port conflict: 5000 was never available</h2>
        <p>
            The plan specifies the registry on <strong>port 5000</strong> in both &sect;3b and
            the Phase A section. On .199 that port is already published by the
            <code>comserv2-web-prod</code> container; 3000, 4000, 8081, 8083 and 11434 are
            likewise occupied. Freeing 5000 would require stopping a live application
            container, which standing operational rules forbid. The registry will therefore
            publish host port <strong>5001</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
            The durable mitigation is naming, not the port number. A registry's address
            becomes part of every image name, so an IP-and-port baked into tags propagates
            into compose files, manifests, deploy scripts and every node's
            <code>insecure-registries</code> list. The plan now mandates
            <code>comserv-registry.lan:5001</code> as the single canonical name, recorded in
            <code>services.json</code>, so relocating the registry later is a DNS change
            rather than a repo-wide rewrite. The plan also now warns that the
            <code>insecure-registries</code> value must match the image-name string byte for
            byte &mdash; an IP and a hostname are not interchangeable to the Docker daemon,
            and mixing them produces a failure that reads like a TLS bug but is not one.
        </p>

        <h2>&sect;8 blast radius corrected</h2>
        <p>
            The retained-SPOF list claimed that losing the registry means &ldquo;only new
            deploys stop&rdquo;. That understates it: a pod <em>rescheduled</em> onto a node
            without the image cached cannot start while the registry is down, so a node
            failure during a registry outage does not self-heal. The two faults compound.
            &sect;8 now states this, with the <code>docker save | ssh host docker load</code>
            escape hatch and the second-home requirement tracked in todo
            <a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %&#93;?record_id=2044">#2044</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Todos created under sub-project #244</h2>
        <table style="width:100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: var(--spacing-medium) 0;">
            <tr style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.12);">
                <th style="text-align:left; padding:6px;">Todo</th>
                <th style="text-align:left; padding:6px;">Work</th>
            </tr>
            <tr><td style="padding:6px;"><a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %&#93;?record_id=2037">#2037</a></td><td style="padding:6px;">A.0 ROLE EVAL &mdash; answered, .199 on disk evidence</td></tr>
            <tr><td style="padding:6px;"><a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %&#93;?record_id=2038">#2038</a></td><td style="padding:6px;">A.1 DEPENDENCY &mdash; not blocked; LAN-only HTTP needs no credentials</td></tr>
            <tr><td style="padding:6px;"><a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %&#93;?record_id=2039">#2039</a></td><td style="padding:6px;">A.2 Disk headroom confirmed; growth estimate owed to A.6</td></tr>
            <tr><td style="padding:6px;"><a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %&#93;?record_id=2040">#2040</a></td><td style="padding:6px;">A.3 Stand up <code>registry:2</code> on 5001 with <code>comserv2_registry_data</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td style="padding:6px;"><a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %&#93;?record_id=2041">#2041</a></td><td style="padding:6px;">A.4 <code>insecure-registries</code> + canonical name &mdash; needs authorization on .126</td></tr>
            <tr><td style="padding:6px;"><a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %&#93;?record_id=2042">#2042</a></td><td style="padding:6px;">A.5 Push/pull round trip with digest evidence &mdash; the gate</td></tr>
            <tr><td style="padding:6px;"><a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %&#93;?record_id=2043">#2043</a></td><td style="padding:6px;">A.6 Retention / pruning policy</td></tr>
            <tr><td style="padding:6px;"><a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %&#93;?record_id=2044">#2044</a></td><td style="padding:6px;">A.7 Registry-down failover and escape hatch</td></tr>
        </table>
    </section>

    <section class="changelog-details">
        <h2>Still open &mdash; requires explicit authorization</h2>
        <p>
            Todo <a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %&#93;?record_id=2041">#2041</a> (A.4)
            cannot complete without restarting <code>dockerd</code> on .126 so it picks up
            <code>insecure-registries</code>, and that restarts the live
            <code>comserv2-web-prod</code> container. That crosses the never-start-stop-the-app
            rule and must be scheduled deliberately with the user, not taken opportunistically.
            Gate todo <a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %&#93;?record_id=1905">#1905</a>
            therefore stays open until the A.5 digest round trip is demonstrated.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="changelog-related">
        <h2>Related</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/Documentation/K3S_APP_HA_PLAN') %&#93;">Availability &amp; Load Balancing Master Plan</a> &mdash; updated to v1.11 (&sect;3d-i, &sect;3d-ii, Phase A, &sect;8)</li>
            <li><a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/project/details') %&#93;?project_id=202">Project #202 (INFRA-HA)</a></li>
            <li><a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/project/details') %&#93;?project_id=244">Sub-project #244 (INFRA-HA-A)</a></li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
</div>
<div id="2026-08-10-model-dropdown-price-display" class="cl-entry">
<h3>AI Model Dropdown &amp;mdash; Show per-token Price</h3>
&#91;% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %&#93;&#91;% PageVersion %&#93;&#91;% END %&#93;







<div class="changelog-entry">
    <header class="changelog-header">
        <h1>AI Model Dropdown &mdash; Show per-token Price</h1>
        <div class="changelog-meta">
            <span class="date">August 10, 2026</span>
            <span class="author">by shanta</span>
            <span class="type">Feature / AIMPS-P2 (#254)</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="changelog-summary">
        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <p>
            The shared model <code>&lt;select&gt;</code> (rendered by
            <code>ai/model_select.tt</code> &mdash; the single source of truth used by the
            floating &ldquo;Chat with AI&rdquo; widget, <code>/ai</code>, <code>/ai2</code> and
            the AI2 editor) now shows the real per-token cost for paid models, drawn from
            the pricing feed delivered in AIMPS-P1 (#253). The user sees what a choice
            costs <em>before</em> picking it.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="changelog-details">
        <h2>What changed</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>In <code>ai/model_select.tt</code>, the cost marker block now renders for
                paid (or any priced) model:
                <code>$&lt;price_prompt&gt;/$&lt;price_completion&gt; per 1M (&lt;price_tier&gt;)</code>,
                e.g. <code>$0.10/$0.40 per 1M (cheap)</code> for Gemini 2.0 Flash or
                <code>$3.00/$15.00 per 1M (premium)</code> for Claude 3.5 Sonnet.</li>
            <li>Free models still read <code>— free</code>; Ollama still reads
                <code>— local</code>. The existing free-first / alphabetical ordering is
                unchanged.</li>
            <li>The cost is formatted with the TT <code>format('%.2f')</code> filter
                (already used across payment / 3d / ai templates in this app). Note:
                <code>sprintf</code> and <code>int()</code> are <em>not</em> available as
                TT functions/methods in this build, so <code>format</code> is the correct
                tool &mdash; verified by render test, not assumption.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Correction &mdash; the widget is JS-rendered, not server-rendered</h2>
        <p>
            The original note claimed the widget reuses the server-rendered
            <code>&lt;select&gt;</code> and needs no JS change. That was <strong>wrong</strong>.
            <code>ai-chat/model-select.js</code> is what actually builds the dropdown for the
            floating widget, <code>/ai</code>, <code>/ai2</code> and the git dashboard: on
            <code>init()</code> it does <code>selectEl.innerHTML = ''</code> and rebuilds options
            from <code>window.ComservConfig.models</code>. Two bugs followed:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>No price in the widget:</strong> <code>fromFlat()</code> mapped only
                <code>{value,label,provider}</code> and threw away <code>price_prompt</code> /
                <code>price_completion</code> / <code>pricing</code>, and <code>render()</code>
                never appended a cost marker. Fixed: carry the price fields through
                <code>fromFlat()</code> and append
                <code>— $pp/$pc per 1M (tier)</code> / <code>— free</code> / <code>— local</code>
                in <code>render()</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Doubled provider name:</strong> the catalog <code>label</code> already
                contained the provider (e.g. <code>Cohere: North Mini Code (free) (openrouter)</code>)
                and the option was grouped under an <code>OpenRouter</code> optgroup header,
                so the provider showed twice. Fixed by stripping the trailing
                <code>(provider)</code> suffix from the label in <code>render()</code> (the
                optgroup header is the single source of truth for the provider).</li>
            <li><strong><code>/ai</code> / git showed no list (or empty):</strong> those pages
                never emitted <code>window.ComservConfig.models</code>, so
                <code>model-select.js</code> fell back to a <code>/ai2/providers</code> fetch
                (slow, and the grouped shape drops price). Fixed by emitting the global on
                <code>/ai</code> and <code>/ai2</code> (from the stash, like the widget) and in
                the <code>/admin/git</code> block of <code>js_load.tt</code>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            The server-rendered <code>ai/model_select.tt</code> still renders correctly for any
            surface that uses it directly; the JS fix is what the user actually sees in the
            widget and the AI pages.
        </p>

        <h2>Verified</h2>
        <p>
            Live browser render of the floating widget (and the shared
            <code>model-select.js</code> path) now shows:
            <code>AI21: Jamba Large 1.7 (openrouter) — $2.00/$8.00 per 1M (premium)</code>,
            <code>AllenAI: Olmo 3 32B Think (openrouter) — $0.15/$0.50 per 1M (cheap)</code>,
            <code>gemma4-64k:latest — local</code>,
            <code>NVIDIA: Nemotron 3 Nano 30B A3B (free) (openrouter) — free</code>.
            Provider name appears once (optgroup header), no longer doubled. The
            <code>/ai</code> page now emits the 414-model catalog global (382 priced).
        </p>

        <h2>Remaining P2 work (still open)</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Premium-tier &ldquo;show all models&rdquo; toggle (the full OpenRouter list is
                long and not a usable default dropdown).</li>
            <li>Tier-then-capability ordering to replace the current
                free-first-then-alphabetical sort.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Files changed</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>root/ai/model_select.tt</code> &mdash; render price + tier on paid models (server path)</li>
            <li><code>root/static/js/ai-chat/model-select.js</code> &mdash; carry price through <code>fromFlat</code>, append cost marker + de-dupe provider in <code>render</code></li>
            <li><code>root/ai/index.tt</code>, <code>root/ai2/index.tt</code> &mdash; emit <code>ComservConfig.models</code> global (fast path)</li>
            <li><code>root/js_load.tt</code> &mdash; emit the global on <code>/admin/git</code> (convention: no inline JS in templates)</li>
            <li><code>root/Documentation/AIModelPresentationPlan.tt</code> &mdash; mark P2 price display delivered</li>
            <li><code>root/Documentation/changelog/2026-08-10-model-dropdown-price-display.tt</code> &mdash; this entry</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
</div>
<div id="2026-08-10-model-role-filter" class="cl-entry">
<h3>AI Model List — Role-based visibility (guests see free tier only)</h3>
&#91;% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %&#93;&#91;% PageVersion %&#93;&#91;% END %&#93;







<div class="changelog-entry">
    <header class="changelog-header">
        <h1>AI model list — role-based visibility</h1>
        <div class="changelog-meta">
            <span class="date">August 10, 2026</span>
            <span class="author">by shanta</span>
            <span class="type">Feature / AIMPS Phase 3 (#255)</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="changelog-summary">
        <p>
            The shared model catalog (<code>Comserv::Util::ModelCatalog</code>) previously
            returned the <strong>entire</strong> list &mdash; every paid OpenRouter model plus
            Grok &mdash; to every caller, including not-logged-in users (the floating
            &ldquo;Chat with AI&rdquo; widget is visible to guests). A guest therefore saw the
            same 400+ model list an admin sees. Now the catalog is <strong>role-filtered</strong>
            at the single source of truth, so each role gets its own shortlist (AIMPS Phase 3
            &mdash; role-scoped shortlists).
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="changelog-details">
        <h2>Visibility tiers</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>guest / anonymous</strong> &mdash; free tier only: free OpenRouter
                models (<code>:free</code> slugs) + Ollama local. No paid models, no Grok.</li>
            <li><strong>member</strong> (logged in, non-privileged) &mdash; free + cheap + mid.
                Premium models (dearer side &gt; $5 / 1M tokens) and Grok are excluded.</li>
            <li><strong>privileged</strong> (admin / developer / editor) &mdash; the full catalog.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            The unfiltered list stays in the process cache; filtering is applied per request in
            <code>catalog()</code> / <code>catalog_json()</code> (cheap, ~414 entries). This means
            <code>window.ComservConfig.models</code> (the global the widget, <code>/ai</code>,
            <code>/ai2</code> and the git dashboard all render from) is already role-filtered, so
            no per-surface JS change was needed.
        </p>

        <h2>Verified</h2>
        <p>
            Live unauthenticated request to <code>/ai/widget</code> now returns
            <strong>19 models</strong> (5 Ollama local + 14 free OpenRouter), with
            <strong>0 paid</strong> and <strong>0 Grok</strong> visible &mdash; down from the full
            414-model admin list. Privileged sessions still receive the full catalog.
            <code>perl -c</code> on ModelCatalog passes.
        </p>

        <h2>Files changed</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Util/ModelCatalog.pm</code> &mdash; add <code>_role_tier</code> +
                <code>_filter_for_role</code>; <code>catalog</code> / <code>catalog_json</code> now
                return the role-filtered list</li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/AI2/Router.pm</code> &mdash; apply the SAME role filter
                at <code>get_available_models</code> (the single source of truth), so every
                consumer (ModelCatalog, <code>/ai2/providers</code>, widget, <code>/ai</code>,
                git dashboard) is filtered with NO per-list re-implementation. This is the
                &ldquo;high in the tree&rdquo; placement the user asked for.</li>
            <li><code>root/Documentation/changelog/2026-08-10-model-role-filter.tt</code> &mdash; this entry</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
</div>
<div id="2026-08-10-openrouter-pricing-feed" class="cl-entry">
<h3>OpenRouter Pricing Feed &amp;mdash; Keep per-token cost from /api/v1/models</h3>
&#91;% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %&#93;&#91;% PageVersion %&#93;&#91;% END %&#93;







<div class="changelog-entry">
    <header class="changelog-header">
        <h1>OpenRouter Pricing Feed &mdash; Keep per-token cost</h1>
        <div class="changelog-meta">
            <span class="date">August 10, 2026</span>
            <span class="author">by shanta</span>
            <span class="type">Feature / AIMPS-P1 (#253)</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="changelog-summary">
        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <p>
            <code>Provider::OpenRouter::list_models</code> previously mapped each model to
            only <code>{ id, label }</code> and threw away the <code>pricing</code> object
            that OpenRouter returns from <code>/api/v1/models</code>. The real per-token
            cost is now kept and carried all the way through to the shared model catalog,
            so every AI surface can sort, filter and display by actual price. This
            completes Phase 1 of
            <a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/Documentation/AIModelPresentationPlan') %&#93;">AI Model
            Presentation &amp; Selection</a> (project 252, sub-project 253).
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="changelog-details">
        <h2>What changed</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong><code>Provider::OpenRouter::list_models</code></strong> now keeps the
                raw <code>pricing</code> hash and adds <code>price_prompt</code> and
                <code>price_completion</code> as USD-per-1M-token numbers. OpenRouter reports
                per-token prices as strings (<code>"0.000001"</code>); the new
                <code>_per_million</code> helper converts them to per-1M USD and returns
                <code>0</code> for anything missing or non-numeric.</li>
            <li><strong><code>Model::AI2::Router::get_available_models</code></strong> carries
                <code>pricing</code>, <code>price_prompt</code> and
                <code>price_completion</code> on each OpenRouter model it emits (the
                <code>:free</code> slugs carry a zero pricing hash).</li>
            <li><strong><code>Model::Util::ModelCatalog::_flatten</code></strong> exposes
                <code>price_prompt</code>, <code>price_completion</code> and a new
                <code>price_tier</code> on every catalog entry. The tier is
                <strong>threshold-derived</strong> (never a hardcoded model list, which
                would rot as the catalog changes weekly):
                <ul>
                    <li><code>free</code> &mdash; zero per-token cost</li>
                    <li><code>cheap</code> &mdash; dearer side &le; $1 / 1M tokens</li>
                    <li><code>mid</code> &mdash; dearer side &le; $5 / 1M tokens</li>
                    <li><code>premium</code> &mdash; dearer side &gt; $5 / 1M tokens</li>
                </ul>
                Tiers are ranked by the dearer of prompt/completion so a model is not
                under-classified when only its output price is high.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Verified</h2>
        <p>
            All three modules pass <code>perl -c</code>. A standalone harness fed sample
            OpenRouter pricing through the real <code>_flatten</code> /
            <code>_price_tier</code> path and produced the expected tiers:
            <code>:free</code> &rarr; <code>free</code>; Gemini 2.0 Flash ($0.1/$0.4 per 1M)
            &rarr; <code>cheap</code>; GPT-4.1 ($2/$8), Claude 3.5 Sonnet ($3/$15) and
            GPT-4o ($5/$15) &rarr; <code>premium</code>; Ollama &rarr; <code>local</code>
            (tier <code>free</code>, no cash cost).
        </p>

        <h2>Follow-up (phases 2&ndash;5)</h2>
        <p>
            Phases 2&ndash;5 (cost-aware sorting/filtering/price display, page- and
            role-scoped shortlists, usage telemetry, and the standing v2-migration /
            documentation-sync rules) remain tracked in the
            <a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/Documentation/AIModelPresentationPlan') %&#93;">AIMPS plan</a>
            (todos 2023&ndash;2035).
        </p>

        <h2>Follow-up fix (same day): <code>/ai2/providers</code> was stripping pricing</h2>
        <p>
            After P1 landed, the model dropdown still showed the provider (optgroup
            header) but a <strong>blank fee</strong> on every option &mdash; not a browser
            cache issue. Root cause: <code>Controller::AI2::providers</code> rebuilt each
            catalog model as only <code>{ id, label, unreachable }</code> and dropped the
            <code>price_*</code> / <code>pricing</code> fields before calling
            <code>ModelCatalog->prime()</code>, so the shared cache was primed with
            price-less entries and every surface that reads it rendered no cost.
            Fixed by passing <code>price_prompt</code> / <code>price_completion</code> /
            <code>pricing</code> / <code>local</code> through in the <code>providers</code>
            endpoint. Verified live: <code>/ai2/providers</code> returned 399/414 priced
            models and <code>/ai/widget</code> now renders
            <code>AI21: Jamba Large 1.7 &mdash; $2.00/$8.00 per 1M (premium)</code>,
            <code>Ollama &mdash; local</code>, <code>:free &mdash; free</code>, etc.
        </p>

        <h2>Files changed</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/AI2/Provider/OpenRouter.pm</code> &mdash; keep pricing, add <code>_per_million</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/AI2/Router.pm</code> &mdash; carry pricing through <code>get_available_models</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Util/ModelCatalog.pm</code> &mdash; expose <code>price_prompt</code> / <code>price_completion</code> / <code>price_tier</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/AI2.pm</code> &mdash; stop stripping pricing in <code>providers</code> (pass <code>price_*</code> / <code>pricing</code> / <code>local</code> through)</li>
            <li><code>root/Documentation/AIModelPresentationPlan.tt</code> &mdash; mark P1 delivered</li>
            <li><code>root/Documentation/changelog/2026-08-10-openrouter-pricing-feed.tt</code> &mdash; this entry</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
</div>
<div id="2026-08-11-198-probe-and-disk-clear" class="cl-entry">
<h3>INFRA-HA &amp;mdash; .198 probed, disk cleared, 3rd node unlocked</h3>
<div class="container">
    <h1 class="doc-h1">INFRA-HA &mdash; .198 probed, disk cleared, 3rd node unlocked</h1>

    <div class="doc-muted last-updated">
        Last Updated: 2026-08-11 | Version: 1.00 | Author: shanta | Status: Infrastructure change (cleanup only, no app container touched)
    </div>

    <div id="toc" class="row doc-toc">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">Quick Navigation</h2>
            <div class="doc-navrow">
                <a href="#summary" class="doc-navlink">Summary</a>
                <a href="#probe" class="doc-navlink">What .198 actually is</a>
                <a href="#disk" class="doc-navlink">Disk cleanup</a>
                <a href="#plan" class="doc-navlink">Plan corrections</a>
                <a href="#next" class="doc-navlink">What unblocks</a>
                <a href="#tracking" class="doc-navlink">Project Tracking</a>
                <a href="#see-also" class="doc-navlink">See Also</a>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="summary" class="doc-h2">1. Summary</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">
                The master plan (v1.12) carried three false claims about
                <strong>.198</strong>: (a) it "could not be probed (different SSH credentials)",
                (b) it was the "Backup DB server", and (c) Phase F.0 was therefore blocked on
                a credentials dependency. All three are now disproven by direct investigation on
                2026-08-11. .198 shares the <em>same</em> SSH credentials as .199, is <em>not</em>
                the production database, and its root disk &mdash; which was 100% full &mdash; was
                filled with personal data, not the DB. The disk was cleared and the 2024 backups
                were preserved. .198 is now a credible <strong>third app node</strong>, which
                directly closes the &sect;3e quorum gap in the plan. No application container was
                started, stopped, or modified.
            </p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="probe" class="doc-h2">2. What .198 actually is (verified)</h2>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">Property</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Plan v1.12 said</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Verified 2026-08-11</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">SSH credentials</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">"different from .126; must be supplied by user"</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><strong>Same as .199</strong> (key auth works); probed successfully</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">Docker</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">"status could not be probed"</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><strong>v29.7.2 installed, daemon active</strong>, 0 containers</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Database role</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">"Backup DB server (MySQL/MariaDB on 3306)"</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">MariaDB present but holds <strong>zero application schemas</strong> (~377M system only); not the Comserv primary (.20:3307 is). Clean replica base, not a conflicting primary.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">Disk</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">(unverified)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Was <strong>100% full (156G/164G, 61M free)</strong>; root cause was /home/shanta (102G personal) and /snap (42G), not the DB. Now <strong>32G free</strong> after cleanup.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">RAM / DB reachability</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">(unverified)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">15 GB RAM free; can reach primary DB at <strong>.20:3307</strong> (confirmed by TCP probe).</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="disk" class="doc-h2">3. Disk cleanup performed (conservative, reversible where possible)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Ran read-only-then-delete on .198 with the user's explicit go-ahead. The only "live" file touched was truncated, not deleted; the only data of possible value was copied off-box first.</p>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Truncated</strong> a 4.6 GB runaway <code>/home/shanta/nohup.out</code> log (live, so truncated not removed) &mdash; freed ~4.6 GB immediately.</li>
                <li><strong>Removed</strong> regenerable caches/crash dumps: <code>~/.codeium</code> (2.3 GB), <code>java_error_in_pycharm.hprof</code> (2.7 GB), <code>~/.cache</code> (Raspberry Pi Imager cache).</li>
                <li><strong>Removed</strong> clearly-stale 2023 download tarballs (<code>beemast</code>, <code>iamnuts</code>) from <code>~/Downloads</code>.</li>
                <li><strong>Preserved</strong> the "possibly important" 2024 <code>~/backups/comserv-24-04-01</code> (16 GB) by rsync-ing the full set to <code>.199:/home/shanta/comserv2-backups-198-2024</code> for safekeeping, then deleted the originals on .198.</li>
                <li><strong>Did NOT touch</strong> MariaDB data, the NFS-exported comserv2 repo, or any file outside the listed junk.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="doc-info">
                <h3>Note on NFS &mdash; corrected</h3>
                <p class="doc-body">The user mentioned an NFS server "to move important files to". Investigation found .198 <em>is</em> an NFS <em>server</em> (its <code>/etc/exports</code> lists the comserv2 repo shared to .199) but that export is currently <strong>dormant</strong> (nfs-server service not running) and is a dev code-share, <strong>not</strong> the app's shared-data NFS. The application's real shared-data NFS is <strong>192.168.1.175</strong> (<code>/mnt/data</code>), mounted at <code>/data/nfs</code> inside containers via the <code>workshop-files-nfs</code> volume in <code>docker-compose.prod.yml</code> (<code>type: nfs, o: addr=192.168.1.175,...,device: ":/"</code>). The 2024 backups were therefore relocated via rsync to .199 rather than NFS. Nothing on the live repo was affected.</p>
                <p class="doc-body"><strong>Implication for new nodes:</strong> a .198 (or .126) app node gets <code>/data/nfs</code> automatically <em>only if</em> it is deployed via the same compose/k8s spec that declares <code>workshop-files-nfs</code> AND (a) it can route to .175:2049 and (b) .175's <code>/etc/exports</code> permits that node's IP. The NFS mount travels with the deployment spec, not the image. See Phase C / Phase F NFS prerequisite.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="plan" class="doc-h2">4. Master plan corrections (v1.12 &rarr; v1.13)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">The authoritative plan <a href="/Documentation/K3S_APP_HA_PLAN">Availability &amp; Load Balancing Master Plan</a> was updated to match this evidence:</p>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li>&sect;2 "Verified current state" &mdash; .198 row rewritten: Docker active, 32 GB free, viable 3rd app node. The "different credentials / unverified" standing constraint replaced with the corrected record.</li>
                <li>&sect;3e "How many nodes?" &mdash; the "honest gap: no credible third node" paragraph replaced: .198 is now a real, owned, in-rack third node; B.2 topology should default to <strong>3 nodes (.126 / .199 / .198)</strong>.</li>
                <li>Phase F (DB HA) &mdash; F.0 unblocked: .198 shares .199 creds and was probed; on-box MariaDB is a clean replica base. AUTH-R4 downgraded from blocker to recommendation.</li>
                <li>&sect;8 retained SPOFs &mdash; .198 noted as the dedicated third node resolving the ".199 is the workstation" tension; OPNsense named as the remaining SPOF once the app tier is 3-node behind it.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="next" class="doc-h2">5. What this unblocks</h2>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">Previously blocked</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Now</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Phase B.2 topology decision (2 vs 3 nodes)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">3-node embedded-etcd HA control plane is a low-cost, owned-hardware option &mdash; no quorum gap.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">Phase F.0 DB replica assessment (AUTH-R4 credentials)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">.198 reachable; F.0 can proceed to version-parity + drift check.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">App-tier SPOF on .199 workstation</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">A dedicated .198 app node means the site no longer depends on the workstation staying up.</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-body"><strong>Still requires explicit authorization before any change:</strong> standing up the registry on .199 (Phase A.3/A.4), any k3s install, OPNsense HAProxy changes, and DB replication. This entry is investigation + cleanup + documentation only.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="tracking" class="doc-h2">Project Tracking</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">
                Owning project:
                <a href="/project/details?project_id=202" class="doc-link">#202 (INFRA-HA)</a>.
                Each phase is a sub-project of #202. This entry updates the plan text only;
                no new phase todos were created &mdash; it clears blockers on existing ones
                (Phase B.2 topology, Phase F.0/F.1).
            </p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <div id="see-also" class="doc-success">
                <h2 class="doc-h3">6. See Also</h2>
                <ul class="doc-body">
                    <li><a href="/Documentation/K3S_APP_HA_PLAN" class="doc-link">Availability &amp; Load Balancing Master Plan</a> &mdash; updated to v1.13 (&sect;2, &sect;3e, Phase F, &sect;8)</li>
                    <li><a href="/Documentation/2026-08-10-infra-ha-phase-a-registry-decomposition" class="doc-link">Changelog 2026-08-10 (a)</a> &mdash; Phase A decomposition, registry port 5001</li>
                    <li><a href="/Documentation/GatewayPlan" class="doc-link">Gateway Plan</a> &mdash; OPNsense HAProxy + ACME, the LB entry point for the 3-node tier</li>
                    <li><a href="/project/details?project_id=202" class="doc-link">Project #202 (INFRA-HA)</a> &mdash; live phase tracking</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="2026-08-11-auto-db-info-cache-and-poll-guard" class="cl-entry">
<h3>Per-request CPU storm &amp;mdash; static DB info cached + chat polling loops made idempotent</h3>
&#91;% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %&#93;&#91;% PageVersion %&#93;&#91;% END %&#93;







<div class="changelog-entry">
    <header class="changelog-header">
        <h1>Per-request CPU storm &mdash; static DB info cached, polling loops idempotent</h1>
        <div class="changelog-meta">
            <span class="date">August 11, 2026</span>
            <span class="author">by shanta</span>
            <span class="type">Performance / Bug Fix</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="changelog-summary">
        <p>
            The workstation CPU spiked to ~99% (load 11.6, 20 starman workers CPU-spinning in
            <code>state=R</code>). Two coupled causes, both now fixed:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Server:</strong> <code>Controller/Root.pm::auto</code> re-derived the
                static DB-connection info (<code>get_connection_info</code> &mdash; a fixed config
                hash) and re-ran <code>get_all_sites</code> (a full DB query + 17 log lines) on
                <em>every</em> request, even though the DB location is known and never changes per
                request. As the user put it: &ldquo;why is the code repeatedly scanning for db when
                it already knows the only location it exists.&rdquo;</li>
            <li><strong>Client:</strong> <code>root/static/js/ai-chat/support.js</code> added a
                fresh pair of <code>setInterval</code> poll loops (<code>chat/admin_heartbeat</code>,
                <code>chat/pending_count</code>) on every <code>DOMContentLoaded</code> without ever
                clearing the previous ones. When the chat widget re-initialised repeatedly, the loops
                <em>stacked</em> into a self-inflicted flood (~12,000 req/min from a single browser
                tab), each request paying the full redundant <code>auto</code> cost.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="changelog-details">
        <h2>Why multiple tabs are fine, but stacking is not</h2>
        <p>
            Separate browser tabs are separate clients/sessions; each legitimately runs one poll loop
            &mdash; that is correct and was never the problem. The defect was <em>one page
            accumulating many loops</em> because the script kept adding intervals without removing
            old ones. On a multi-domain production host the same stacking would multiply across
            re-initialisations and collapse the box quickly, which is exactly why it had to be fixed
            at the source rather than just closing the tab.
        </p>

        <h2>Fix</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Root.pm</code> &mdash; caches the resolved
                DB-connection list + host per worker (5-minute TTL), following the existing
                <code>$_remotedb_status</code> precedent already in the file. Cache hits skip all
                model/DB work in <code>auto</code>. The data is identical for every domain a process
                serves, so this is correct on a multi-domain production host.</li>
            <li><code>root/static/js/ai-chat/support.js</code> &mdash; extracted the admin notifier
                start into <code>_scheduleAdminNotifier()</code>, which clears any existing timers
                before (re)starting. Re-running the script can never stack additional loops. One poll
                loop per page, exactly as intended (initial 2s poll + 30s pending + 20s heartbeat).</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Verified</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>perl -c</code> clean on <code>Controller/Root.pm</code>.</li>
            <li><code>node --check</code> clean on <code>ai-chat/support.js</code>.</li>
            <li>Standalone app (3001) auto-reloads <code>.pm</code>/<code>.js</code>; a fresh page
                load now runs one poll loop.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Files changed</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Root.pm</code> &mdash; per-worker DB-connection cache + guarded <code>auto</code> gather</li>
            <li><code>root/static/js/ai-chat/support.js</code> &mdash; idempotent <code>_scheduleAdminNotifier()</code></li>
            <li><code>root/Documentation/changelog/2026-08-11-auto-db-info-cache-and-poll-guard.tt</code> &mdash; this entry</li>
            <li><code>root/Documentation/changelog/CHANGELOG.tt</code> &mdash; [Unreleased] bullet cross-linked here</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Related</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="&#91;% c.uri_for('/Documentation/changelog/2026-08-10-ai2-providers-hashref-guard') %&#93;">AI2 Providers &mdash; guard against malformed catalog elements</a></li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
</div>
<div id="2026-08-12-api-focus-models-namespace-autoclean-fix" class="cl-entry">
<h3>Api::api_focus_models namespace::autoclean Try::Tiny Fix - August 12, 2026</h3>
<div class="container">
    <h1 class="doc-h1">Api::api_focus_models Fix &mdash; namespace::autoclean + Try::Tiny &mdash; August 12, 2026</h1>

    <div class="doc-muted last-updated">
        Last Updated: 2026-08-12 |
        Version: 0.01 |
        Author: Hermes Agent |
        Status: Fixed
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="overview" class="doc-h2">1. Issue</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">
                The error-audit system logged repeated <code>ERROR</code> entries from
                <code>Comserv::Controller::Api->api_focus_models</code>:
            </p>
            <div class="doc-codebox">
                <pre><code>[GLOBAL ERROR] Unhandled exception: Caught exception in
Comserv::Controller::Api->api_focus_models "Can't call method "catch"
on an undefined value at .../lib/Comserv/Controller/Api.pm line 1930."
Path: api/focus/models  IP: 192.168.1.199  Referer: /planning/daily</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-body">
                The reported line number (1930) was from the 2026-08-10 code; that block has
                since been refactored to <code>eval {...}</code> and is fine. The real live
                defect is a genuine <code>try { } catch { }</code> block at lines 1003&ndash;1013
                inside the local-auth user resolver (<code>_api_get_user_context</code>) that runs
                before <code>api_focus_models</code>. The <code>192.168.1.199</code> IP is exactly
                the local-network path that hits this code, so it crashed on every local request
                to <code>/api/focus/models</code>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="root-cause" class="doc-h2">2. Root Cause</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">
                <code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Api.pm</code> declared:
            </p>
            <div class="doc-codebox">
                <pre><code>use namespace::autoclean;</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-body">
                with no <code>-except</code> guard. Under Perl 5.40, <code>namespace::autoclean</code>
                strips the <code>try</code>/<code>catch</code> keywords that <code>Try::Tiny</code>
                injected at compile time. The <code>try { ... } catch { ... }</code> block then
                degrades to <code>try{...}->catch(...)</code> on an undefined value &mdash; yielding
                precisely the "Can't call method 'catch' on an undefined value" exception. This is
                the same class of bug already fixed in <code>ThemeConfig.pm</code> and documented in
                the project's Perl 5.40 notes.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="solution" class="doc-h2">3. Solution</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">
                Added the <code>-except</code> clause so the Try::Tiny keywords survive cleanup,
                matching the established pattern already used in <code>ThemeConfig.pm</code>:
            </p>
            <div class="doc-codebox">
                <pre><code># before
use namespace::autoclean;
# after
use namespace::autoclean -except => [qw(try catch finally)];  # keep Try::Tiny subs (Perl 5.40)</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-body">
                No other code in <code>Api.pm</code> needed changing &mdash; the single remaining
                <code>try/catch</code> block is now correctly resolved at runtime.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="scope" class="doc-h2">4. Scope Note</h2>
            <div class="doc-warning">
                <p class="doc-body">
                    The same latent defect exists in other controllers that combine a bare
                    <code>use namespace::autoclean;</code> with real <code>try { } catch { }</code>
                    usage: <code>HostingSignup.pm</code> and <code>3d.pm</code> (genuine
                    Try::Tiny blocks). A broader sweep (13 files match the text) was deferred
                    pending user confirmation. Those two should get the same <code>-except</code>
                    guard before their code paths are exercised on Perl 5.40.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="files" class="doc-h2">5. Files Modified</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Controller/Api.pm</code> &mdash; added
                    <code>-except => [qw(try catch finally)]</code> to the
                    <code>namespace::autoclean</code> import (line 3).</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="testing" class="doc-h2">6. Verification</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>perl -Mlib=lib -c lib/Comserv/Controller/Api.pm</code> &rarr; syntax OK.</li>
                <li>Confirmed the only <code>try</code>/<code>catch</code> pair in the file is the
                    local-auth block at 1003&ndash;1013, which now resolves via the <code>-except</code> guard.</li>
                <li>Standing rule respected: the app was not started/stopped and
                    <code>comserv_server.pl</code> was not modified. The fix is effective on the
                    next code reload / deploy.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="see-also" class="doc-h2">7. See Also</h2>
            <div class="doc-success">
                <ul class="doc-body">
                    <li><a href="/Documentation/changelog#2026-08-12-themeconfig-missing-dir-fix" class="doc-link">ThemeConfig set_site_theme ENOENT Fix</a> &mdash; sibling fix in the same audit window.</li>
                    <li><a href="/Documentation/ThemeConfig" class="doc-link">Theme Configuration</a> &mdash; example of the same <code>-except</code> guard already applied.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="2026-08-12-daily-plan-guide-master-plan" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-08-12 — Planning tab renamed MASTER PLAN + master plan now displays reliably</h3>
<h2>2026-08-12 — MASTER PLAN tab: rename + reliable display</h2>

<p><strong>What changed:</strong></p>
<ul>
    <li>The CSC-only tab on <code>/planning/daily</code> was relabelled <strong>MASTER PLAN</strong> (was <em>DAILY PLAN GUIDE</em>).</li>
    <li>The tab already <code>INCLUDE</code>s <a href="/Documentation/MASTER_PLAN">Documentation/MASTER_PLAN.tt</a>, so switching to it displays the current master plan, scoped by SiteName.</li>
    <li><strong>Display fix:</strong> the master-plan content is server-rendered into <code>#daily-plan-guide</code>, but it was hidden by
        <code>.tab-content { display: none }</code> until JS added <code>.active</code> via the URL <code>#daily-plan-guide</code> hash.
        Activation ran only on <code>window.load</code>, so a slow/stalled deferred script (or <code>load</code> already fired)
        left the tab blank with no content. Hardened so the plan always shows:
        <ul>
            <li><code>daily-plan.css</code> — <code>#daily-plan-guide</code> is <code>display:block</code> by default (server-rendered, always safe to show); a <code>.tab-hidden</code> helper class hides it when another tab is chosen.</li>
            <li><code>daily-plan-utils.js</code> — <code>switchTab()</code> now toggles <code>.tab-hidden</code> on the guide tab (hidden when another tab is active, shown when selected), and hash-tab activation also runs on <code>DOMContentLoaded</code> + <code>hashchange</code> (not only <code>window.load</code>).</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<p><strong>SiteName scoping:</strong> CSC sees the full cross-site roadmap; other sites see a scoped banner. The tab is CSC-only.</p>

<p><strong>Files touched:</strong></p>
<ul>
    <li><code>root/admin/planning/DailyPlan.tt</code> — tab label <code>DAILY PLAN GUIDE</code> → <code>MASTER PLAN</code>; already <code>INCLUDE</code>s the master plan.</li>
    <li><code>root/static/css/planning/daily-plan.css</code> — guide tab visible by default + <code>.tab-hidden</code> helper.</li>
    <li><code>root/static/js/planning/daily-plan-utils.js</code> — <code>switchTab</code> manages guide visibility; hash activation on <code>DOMContentLoaded</code>/<code>hashchange</code>.</li>
    <li><code>root/Documentation/MASTER_PLAN.tt</code> — back-link label updated to <code>MASTER PLAN</code>.</li>
    <li><code>root/Documentation/DailyPlanSystem.tt</code> — implementation note references renamed tab.</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Related:</strong></p>
<ul>
    <li><a href="/planning/daily#daily-plan-guide">Daily Plan · MASTER PLAN</a></li>
    <li><a href="/Documentation/MASTER_PLAN">Comserv2 Master Plan</a></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="2026-08-12-themeconfig-missing-dir-fix" class="cl-entry">
<h3>ThemeConfig set_site_theme ENOENT Fix - August 12, 2026</h3>
<div class="container">
    <h1 class="doc-h1">ThemeConfig set_site_theme ENOENT Fix &mdash; August 12, 2026</h1>

    <div class="doc-muted last-updated">
        Last Updated: 2026-08-12 |
        Version: 0.01 |
        Author: Hermes Agent |
        Status: Fixed
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="overview" class="doc-h2">1. Issue</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">
                The error-audit system logged repeated <code>ERROR</code> entries from
                <code>Comserv::Model::ThemeConfig::set_site_theme</code> (and the sibling
                writers <code>save_theme</code>, <code>create_theme</code>,
                <code>set_site_favicon</code>, <code>set_domain_favicon</code>):
            </p>
            <div class="doc-codebox">
                <pre><code>Error setting theme 'mcoop' for site 'MCoop':
write_file '/opt/comserv/root/static/config/theme_definitions.json' -
sysopen: No such file or directory</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-body">
                This fired on every MCoop index page load because
                <code>Controller/MCoop.pm</code> calls
                <code>set_site_theme($c, "MCoop", "mcoop")</code> on each request.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="root-cause" class="doc-h2">2. Root Cause</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">
                All five writers persisted JSON via <code>File::Slurp::write_file</code> directly.
                <code>write_file</code> does a bare <code>sysopen()</code> and fails with
                <code>ENOENT</code> when the <em>parent directory</em> does not already exist.
                The dev checkout ships <code>root/static/config/</code>, but the production
                container (<code>/opt/comserv/</code>) did not have that directory present, so
                the write could never succeed.
            </p>
            <p class="doc-body">
                Note that the CSS writer <code>_write_theme_css</code> already created its
                directory with <code>File::Path::make_path</code> &mdash; the JSON writers
                simply never got the equivalent guard.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="solution" class="doc-h2">3. Solution</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">
                Added a private helper <code>_ensure_parent_dir($c, $file)</code> that
                <code>mkdir -p</code>s the target file's parent before any write, mirroring
                the pattern already used in <code>_write_theme_css</code>. The helper is now
                called at the start of all five JSON writers:
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>set_site_theme</code> (ThemeConfig.pm)</li>
                <li><code>create_theme</code> (ThemeConfig.pm)</li>
                <li><code>save_theme</code> (ThemeConfig.pm)</li>
                <li><code>set_site_favicon</code> (ThemeConfig.pm)</li>
                <li><code>set_domain_favicon</code> (ThemeConfig.pm)</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-body">
                The directory is now guaranteed to exist regardless of deployment state, so
                the write succeeds on both dev and prod.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="files" class="doc-h2">4. Files Modified</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Model/ThemeConfig.pm</code> &mdash; added
                    <code>_ensure_parent_dir</code> and guarded all five <code>write_file</code> calls.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="testing" class="doc-h2">5. Verification</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>perl -c lib/Comserv/Model/ThemeConfig.pm</code> &rarr; syntax OK.</li>
                <li>Logic review: <code>_ensure_parent_dir</code> returns the existing dir when
                    present (no-op on dev), and creates it when missing (resolves prod ENOENT).</li>
                <li>Sibling call paths (<code>Admin/Theme.pm</code>, <code>ThemeAdmin.pm</code>,
                    <code>MCoop.pm</code>, <code>HostingSignup.pm</code>,
                    <code>SiteProvisioning.pm</code>) are covered through the centralized model fix.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="see-also" class="doc-h2">6. See Also</h2>
            <div class="doc-success">
                <ul class="doc-body">
                    <li><a href="/Documentation/ThemeConfig" class="doc-link">Theme Configuration</a></li>
                    <li><a href="/Documentation/CssThemes" class="doc-link">CSS Theme System &mdash; Admin Guide</a></li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="2026-08-13-daily-plan-remove-duplicate-action-card" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-08-13 — Removed duplicate action bar on /planning/daily; added End Day + Open Logs to the card</h3>
<h2>2026-08-13 — Removed duplicate action bar; added End Day + Open Logs</h2>

<p><strong>What changed:</strong></p>
<ul>
    <li><code>/planning/daily</code> rendered <strong>two</strong> identical action bars:
        <ul>
            <li>a top-level <code>.daily-action-card</code> ("Day Controls") above the tab bar in <code>DailyPlan.tt</code>; and</li>
            <li>a second <code>.ActionBar</code> inside the <strong>Daily Priorities</strong> tab, in <code>_today_work_tab.tt</code>.</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>The second (in-tab) bar was the duplicate. It is hidden on this page via <code>&#91;% INCLUDE 'admin/planning/_today_work_tab.tt' hide_action_bar = 1 %&#93;</code>. The top "Day Controls" card stays as the only action bar on <code>/planning/daily</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Added two buttons to the top card:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>End Day</strong> (<code>data-action="end-day"</code>) — always present (no longer only shown when a log is already open).</li>
            <li><strong>Open Logs</strong> (<code>data-action="toggle-log-panel"</code>) — the alert icon button; it only appears when there is still an open/unclosed log (the original "a log was missed" alert).</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>There are now <strong>two distinct log buttons</strong> on the card (the earlier version had removed the permanent one, causing the glitch):
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Logs</strong> — a permanent link to <code>/log</code>, always present so the user can always check what is still open today.</li>
            <li><strong>Open Logs</strong> (icon) — the conditional alert described above.</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>The card now always shows: Add Todo, All Todos, <strong>Logs</strong>, <strong>Start Day</strong>, <strong>End Day</strong> (admin: Triage Stale, Reschedule); the <strong>Open Logs</strong> icon button appears only when a log is still open, alerting the user that a log was missed.</li>
    <li>The shared inner bar in <code>_today_work_tab.tt</code> is wrapped in <code>&#91;% IF hide_action_bar != 1 %&#93; ... &#91;% END %&#93;</code>, so it still renders normally on the other two pages that include it without the flag (<code>DailyPriorities.tt</code>, <code>DailyPlan.legacy.tt</code>).</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Files touched:</strong></p>
<ul>
    <li><code>root/admin/planning/DailyPlan.tt</code> — pass <code>hide_action_bar = 1</code> to the include; add End Day + Open Logs to the top card (always visible).</li>
    <li><code>root/admin/planning/_today_work_tab.tt</code> — wrap the action bar in <code>&#91;% IF hide_action_bar != 1 %&#93;</code> (no button changes otherwise).</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Related:</strong></p>
<ul>
    <li><a href="/planning/daily">Daily Planning</a></li>
    <li><a href="/planning/daily-priorities">Daily Priorities</a></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="2026-08-13-git-merge-plan-shared-diff-view" class="cl-entry">
<h3>Git merge plan — single shared diff view + mandatory human approve before AI enters main</h3>
<div class="container">

    <h1 class="doc-h1">Git merge plan — single shared diff view + mandatory human approve</h1>

    <div class="last-updated" doc-muted>
        Last Updated: 2026-08-13 | Version: 1.00 | Author: hermes | Status: Plan decision recorded (links to project #238)
    </div>

    <div id="toc" class="row doc-toc">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">Quick Navigation</h2>
            <div class="doc-navrow">
                <a href="#summary" class="doc-navlink">Summary</a>
                <a href="#decisions" class="doc-navlink">Decisions</a>
                <a href="#todos" class="doc-navlink">Linked Todos</a>
                <a href="#files" class="doc-navlink">Files Changed</a>
                <a href="#related" class="doc-navlink">Related</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="summary" class="doc-h2">1. Summary</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Updated <a href="/Documentation/system/git_worktree_merge_plan" class="doc-link">git_worktree_merge_plan.tt</a> from v0.1 → v0.2 to capture two decisions the user made about the git page / review UI:</p>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>One shared diff view.</strong> Created and modified files on the Git Dashboard must each link to a diff view, but there is exactly ONE diff-view component, and every surface (<code>/admin/git</code> working-tree rows, merge review, commit-message preview) links to or embeds it. No per-surface diff fork to maintain. <strong>Correction (2026-08-15):</strong> the original wording here claimed this was "seeded in the AI2 editor <code>git-review.js</code>" — that file never existed. What shipped instead were two bespoke inline renderers: <code>git-dashboard.js</code> (working-tree <code>#git-file-diff</code> panel via <code>GET /admin/git/file_diff</code>) and <code>ai2editor/file-diff.js</code> (<code>#git-diff-pane</code> via <code>GET /ai2/file_diff</code>). On 2026-08-15 the decision was actually implemented: a real canonical widget <code>root/static/js/git-diff-viewer.js</code> (namespace <code>ComservGitDiff</code>) was built and both renderers were refactored to route through it. See <a href="/Documentation/changelog#2026-08-15-git-diff-viewer-shared-widget" class="doc-link">2026-08-15 — shared diff widget built</a>.</li>
                <li><strong>View, edit, approve before AI commits to main.</strong> The AI may commit only inside its worktree. Entry into <code>main</code> requires a human to open the shared diff view, optionally edit files, and record an explicit audit approval that covers the current diff. Merge/push to main are blocked without it.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="decisions" class="doc-h2">2. Decisions locked</h2>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr><th class="doc-th">Topic</th><th class="doc-th">Decision</th><th class="doc-th">Plan section</th></tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Diff viewer architecture</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Single shared component, reused by all surfaces. One page + one code path to maintain. <em>Implemented 2026-08-15 as <code>root/static/js/git-diff-viewer.js</code> (namespace <code>ComservGitDiff</code>); both the dashboard and AI2 editor renderers route through it. See the 2026-08-15 entry.</em></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">§3.5</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Human gate before AI → main</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">View → edit → approve. AI commits only in worktree; merge/push to main blocked until explicit human audit approval covers the diff.</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">§3.6, §6</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="todos" class="doc-h2">3. Linked todos (project #238 GITWT-NEW)</h2>
            <div class="bm-callout" style="border-left: 4px solid var(--primary-color, #2e7d32);">
                <strong>&#128193; All git todos in one place:</strong>
                <a href="/project/details?project_id=238" class="doc-link">Open project #238 (GITWT-NEW)</a>
                for the full, live list of every todo in this work.
            </div>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><a href="/todo/details?record_id=1991" class="doc-link">Todo #1991</a> — Git Desktop: add PyCharm-style per-file diff review and edit workflow. The shared diff view + edit surface (the review surface required before commit).</li>
                <li><a href="/todo/details?record_id=1993" class="doc-link">Todo #1993</a> — Git Desktop: enforce mandatory human audit approval before AI code enters main. The approval gate that blocks merge/push.</li>
                <li><a href="/todo/details?record_id=1992" class="doc-link">Todo #1992</a> — record AI-versus-human commit provenance & changed-file attribution. Shown inside the diff/commit/review screens.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="files" class="doc-h2">4. Files changed in this change</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>root/Documentation/system/git_worktree_merge_plan.tt</code> — v0.2: added <code>project_id</code>/<code>project_code</code> META, §3.5 (single shared diff view), §3.6 (mandatory human approve), and §6 decision log. Cross-linked todos #1991/#1993.</li>
                <li><code>root/Documentation/changelog/2026-08-13-git-merge-plan-shared-diff-view.tt</code> — this entry.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="related" class="doc-h2">5. Related</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><a href="/Documentation/system/git_worktree_merge_plan" class="doc-link">git_worktree_merge_plan.tt</a> (the git page plan this records against).</li>
                <li><a href="/Documentation/system/git_worktree_new_system_plan" class="doc-link">git_worktree_new_system_plan.tt</a> (worktree creation backend, project #238 phases).</li>
                <li><a href="/project/details?project_id=238" class="doc-link">Project #238 (GITWT-NEW)</a>.</li>
            </ul>
