<div id="2026-08-14-planning-daily-focus-queue-fix" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-08-14 — /planning/daily Focus Queue + Start Day button fixes</h3>
<h2>2026-08-14 — <code>/planning/daily</code>: Focus Queue populated + Start Day button works</h2>

<p><strong>Trigger:</strong> an Application Alert fired from <code>Planning.pm sub daily</code>:</p>
<pre>Priority ranking error: Can't locate object method "new" via package "Comserv::Util::TodoRanking"</pre>
<p>The Daily Priorities tab (🎯 Focus Queue) was rendering empty and the planning Projects query was failing — both silently swallowed by <code>eval</code>, so the page still returned HTTP 200.</p>

<h3>Root causes (3 independent bugs in <code>sub daily</code>)</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Focus Queue ranking:</strong> <code>Comserv::Util::TodoRanking-&gt;new</code> — <code>TodoRanking</code> is a <em>procedural</em> module; scoring is the plain sub <code>Comserv::Util::TodoRanking::score_todo($h, $ctx)</code> (no constructor). The call also passed <code>($c, $t)</code> instead of a column hashref + ctx.</li>
    <li><strong>Focus Queue data:</strong> <code>$c-&gt;model('Todo')-&gt;get_all_todos_for_listing($c, $sitename)</code> — that method does not exist on <code>Comserv::Model::Todo</code> (only <code>get_top_todos</code>, <code>get_todos_for_date</code>, <code>get_all_todos_for_calendar</code>, <code>fetch_todo_record</code>). So <code>@all</code> was always empty.</li>
    <li><strong>Planning projects:</strong> <code>$c-&gt;model('Ency')-&gt;resultset('Project')</code> — <code>model('Ency')</code> is not a registered Catalyst model (returns <code>undef</code>), causing <em>"Can't call method resultset on an undefined value"</em>. Every other caller uses <code>model('DBEncy')</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Fixes</h3>
<ul>
    <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Planning.pm</code> — <code>sub daily</code> Focus Queue block rewritten to fetch open (non-done) todos via <code>$schema-&gt;resultset('Todo')-&gt;search(...)</code> (site-filtered), build a <code>%row_by_id</code> column-hash map, score each with the procedural <code>Comserv::Util::TodoRanking::score_todo($h, { now_epoch =&gt; time() })</code>, sort by <code>ap_score</code>, and take the top 20 into <code>@active_priorities</code> (real row objects, as the template expects) with the rest into <code>@remaining_open_todos</code>. Both error paths keep their <code>log_with_details</code> calls (focus query vs focus rank/remaining) so failures still land in <code>application.log</code>.</li>
    <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Planning.pm</code> — planning-projects query changed from <code>model('Ency')</code> to <code>model('DBEncy')</code>.</li>
    <li><code>root/static/js/planning/daily-plan-utils.js</code> — <code>dailyLogAction()</code> made null-safe: the rebuilt <code>DailyPlan.tt</code> index does not carry the old <code>dl-feedback</code> / <code>dl-start-btn</code> / <code>dl-end-btn</code> ids, so <code>feedback.textContent = …</code> threw <code>TypeError</code> before the <code>fetch</code> fired. Every <code>feedback</code>/<code>startBtn</code>/<code>endBtn</code> access is now guarded, so the Start Day / End Day POST always reaches <code>/planning/daily_log</code>.</li>
    <li><code>root/admin/planning/DailyPlan.tt</code> + <code>root/admin/planning/_today_work_tab.tt</code> — added the <code>&lt;span id="dl-feedback"&gt;</code> status node to both action cards so the user sees "Starting…" / success / error inline.</li>
    <li><code>root/static/css/planning/daily-plan.css</code> — added <code>.ActionBarFeedback</code> styling.</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Verification:</strong> <code>perl -c lib/Comserv/Controller/Planning.pm</code> → "syntax OK". No remaining calls to <code>TodoRanking-&gt;new</code>, <code>get_all_todos_for_listing</code>, or <code>model('Ency')</code> in the controller. Static JS/CSS and <code>.tt</code> recompile per request via <code>Module::Refresh</code> on the running <code>:3001</code> process (no restart performed, per ops rules).</p>

<h3>Related</h3>
<ul>
    <li><a href="/planning/daily">Planning · Daily</a> — Daily Priorities tab should now list ranked todos and Start Day should fire.</li>
    <li><a href="/Documentation/MASTER_PLAN">Comserv2 Master Plan</a></li>
    <li><a href="/Documentation/DailyPlanSystem.tt">Daily Plan System</a></li>
</ul>

<hr>

<h2>2026-08-14 (follow-up) — Todo card with HTML in description nested the whole page, killing floating buttons + tab switch</h2>

<p><strong>Symptom (the recurring bug):</strong> on <code>/planning/daily</code>, when todo cards are shown the left-side floating buttons (Back to Top, Edit-with-AI, Chat) disappear and the top tab buttons stop switching tabs. A browser ancestor-chain probe proved the buttons were nested <em>inside</em> a todo card:</p>
<pre>body > div.container > div.tab-content > div.tab-content > div > div.mb-24
  > details.RemainingTodosPanel > div.RemainingTodosBody > div.todo-card
  > details.card > div.card-body > div.mb-2 > div.todo-card-pre > [button]</pre>
<p>That is the page-<strong>duplication</strong> signature: a full second copy of the page (nav, footer, floating buttons) was injected inside one card, collapsing the entire document into a single <code>&lt;details class="card"&gt;</code>. The real body-level buttons were clobbered (<code>#back-to-top NOT in DOM</code>) and tab clicks hit the buried duplicate.</p>

<h3>Root cause</h3>
<ul>
    <li><code>root/todo/todo_card.tt</code> emitted <code>&#91;% tc.description %&#93;</code> and <code>&#91;% tc.comments %&#93;</code> <strong>without the <code>| html</code> escape filter</strong> inside <code>div.todo-card-pre</code>. Any todo whose <code>description</code> (or <code>comments</code>) is itself a full HTML document gets inserted verbatim, nesting the entire page layout inside the card.</li>
    <li>This was dormant until the Focus Queue fix above: <code>@remaining_open_todos</code> was previously always empty, so the <code>RemainingTodosPanel</code> (where the offending card lived) never rendered. Populating the queue exposed the pre-existing template defect.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Fix</h3>
<ul>
    <li><code>root/todo/todo_card.tt</code> — both <code>tc.description</code> and <code>tc.comments</code> now use <code>&#91;% tc.description | html %&#93;</code> / <code>&#91;% tc.comments | html %&#93;</code>. Description text is shown as text, never executed as markup. This protects <em>every</em> card everywhere (todo list, day/week/month, project pages), not just the planning page.</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Verification:</strong> rendered <code>todo/todo_card.tt</code> with a todo whose <code>description</code> is a full <code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;…&lt;nav&gt;…&lt;button class="ai2-float-btn"&gt;…</code> document. After the fix: real <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code> = 0, real <code>&lt;!DOCTYPE&gt;</code> = 0, nested <code>ai2-float-btn</code> button = 0, and the literal markup is present only as escaped <code>&amp;lt;!DOCTYPE html&amp;gt;</code>. The card can no longer nest the page.</p>

<p><strong>Security note:</strong> this was an HTML-injection (stored-XSS-class) defect — a todo description containing attacker-influenced markup would have executed in the viewer's session. Escaping is the correct hardening regardless of the layout symptom.</p>

<hr>

<h2>2026-08-14 (follow-up 2) — Tab switching breaks on Back/Forward (anchor/hash desync)</h2>

<p><strong>Symptom:</strong> on <code>/planning/daily</code>, clicking a tab (Priorities ⇄ Master Plan ⇄ Calendar) shows it correctly, but using the browser <strong>Back button</strong> to return left <em>no tab visible</em> — the page went blank. Identified as a hash/anchor desync, not a CSS or markup error.</p>

<h3>Root cause</h3>
<ul>
    <li><code>switchTab()</code> in <code>root/static/js/planning/daily-plan-utils.js</code> called <code>history.pushState('#'+tabName)</code> on every click, but the script only handled the hash on the initial <code>load</code> event. There was <strong>no <code>popstate</code>/<code>hashchange</code> listener</strong>.</li>
    <li>So: a tab <em>click</em> both shows the panel AND updates the URL hash → works. But browser <strong>Back</strong> reverts the hash (e.g. <code>#calendar</code> → <code>#priorities</code>) with no click, so nothing re-applied <code>.active</code> to any <code>.tab-content</code> → every panel stayed <code>display:none</code> → blank page.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Fix</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Extracted the show/hide into a pure <code>_activateTab(name)</code> helper (removes <code>active</code> from all <code>.tab-content</code>/<code>.tab-button</code>, adds it to the target + matching <code>[data-tab]</code> buttons by selector — robust to non-click callers).</li>
    <li><code>switchTab()</code> now calls <code>_activateTab()</code> then <code>pushState()</code> (unchanged click behaviour).</li>
    <li>Added <code>popstate</code> + <code>hashchange</code> listeners that call <code>_activateTab(location.hash)</code> <strong>without</strong> pushing a new history entry (no duplicate entries / no loop). Now Back/Forward re-shows the correct tab.</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Verification:</strong> <code>node --check root/static/js/planning/daily-plan-utils.js</code> → parse OK. Static JS is served straight from disk (no restart needed). Hard-refresh <code>/planning/daily</code>, click each tab, then press Back/Forward — the correct panel should now always be visible.</p>
</div>
<div id="2026-08-14-planning-daily-tab-anchors-calendar-embed" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-08-14 — /planning/daily tab switching + Calendar tab embed fixes</h3>
<h2>2026-08-14 — <code>/planning/daily</code>: tab return-to-Priorities + Calendar embed</h2>

<h3>Defect 1 — Daily Priorities panel blank when returning to it</h3>
<p><strong>Symptom:</strong> on <code>/planning/daily</code> you could switch TO Master Plan / Calendar, but switching BACK to the 🎯 Daily Priorities tab showed an empty panel. The tab button worked; the content was gone.</p>
<p><strong>Root cause:</strong> the Daily Priorities panel (<code>DailyPlan.tt</code> → <code>id="priorities" class="tab-content active"</code>) INCLUDEs <code>_today_work_tab.tt</code>, whose root element was <code>&lt;div id="today-work" class="tab-content active"&gt;</code>. So the content lived inside a <em>second</em> <code>.tab-content</code>. When <code>_activateTab()</code> in <code>daily-plan-utils.js</code> switches tabs it strips <code>active</code> from <em>every</em> <code>.tab-content</code> and re-adds it only to the matched outer one — the inner <code>#today-work</code> lost its <code>active</code> and, under <code>.tab-content { display: none }</code>, stayed hidden. Returning to priorities re-activated the outer <code>#priorities</code> but never the inner wrapper, so the panel rendered empty.</p>
<p><strong>Fix:</strong> <code>root/admin/planning/_today_work_tab.tt</code> — removed <code>class="tab-content active"</code> from the inner <code>#today-work</code> div (now a plain container). It is already inside one <code>.tab-content</code>, so it no longer fights the tab switcher.</p>

<h3>Defect 2 — Calendar tab loaded the full page, not just the calendar body</h3>
<p><strong>Symptom:</strong> the 📅 Calendar tab showed the entire wrapped page (nav, footer, floating buttons) inside the iframe instead of just the day-calendar body.</p>
<p><strong>Root cause:</strong> the iframe was <code>src="/todo/day/&lt;date&gt;?embed"</code> — a <em>valueless</em> query param. In Catalyst <code>$c-&gt;req-&gt;param('embed')</code> returns <code>''</code> (empty string) for <code>?embed</code>, which is <strong>false</strong>, so the bare-render branch in <code>Todo.pm sub day</code> (<code>if ($c-&gt;req-&gt;param('embed'))</code>) was skipped and <code>day.tt</code> rendered through the normal TT view with <code>layout.tt</code> wrapper — the whole page.</p>
<p><strong>Fixes:</strong></p>
<ul>
    <li><code>root/admin/planning/DailyPlan.tt</code> — iframe <code>src</code> → <code>/todo/day/&lt;date&gt;?embed=1</code> (truthy).</li>
    <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Todo.pm</code> — embed gate changed to <code>if (defined $c-&gt;req-&gt;param('embed'))</code> so any caller (bare or <code>=1</code>) triggers the true bare fragment (no <code>layout.tt</code> wrapper, rendered via a fresh <code>Template-&gt;new</code>).</li>
    <li><code>root/todo/day.tt</code> — <code>is_embed</code> check uses <code>.defined</code> for consistency.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Cleanup — stale monolith anchors (2026-08-13 rename drift)</h3>
<ul>
    <li><code>root/Documentation/MASTER_PLAN.tt</code> — the "← Back to Daily Plan" link pointed at <code>#daily-plan-guide</code>, an id that no longer exists on the rebuilt index (the tab is <code>id="master-plan"</code>). Changed to <code>#master-plan</code>.</li>
    <li><code>root/static/css/planning/daily-plan.css</code> — removed the obsolete <code>#daily-plan-guide { display:block }</code> / <code>.tab-hidden</code> guard that targeted the pre-rebuild monolith id (dead after the rename).</li>
</ul>

<h3>Verification</h3>
<p><code>perl -Ilib -c lib/Comserv/Controller/Todo.pm</code> → "syntax OK". No remaining bare <code>?embed</code> in the live index. Inner <code>#today-work</code> wrapper no longer carries <code>class="tab-content"</code>. Static <code>.tt</code> / <code>.pm</code> recompile per request via <code>Module::Refresh</code> on the running <code>:3001</code> process (no restart performed, per ops rules).</p>

<h3>Related</h3>
<ul>
    <li><a href="/planning/daily">Planning · Daily</a> — Daily Priorities now stays populated on return; Calendar tab shows the bare day calendar.</li>
    <li><a href="/Documentation/MASTER_PLAN">Comserv2 Master Plan</a></li>
    <li><a href="/Documentation/changelog#2026-08-14-planning-daily-focus-queue-fix">2026-08-14 Focus Queue + Start Day fix</a></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="2026-08-15-doc-header-project-link" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-08-15 — Shared doc header INCLUDE with META-driven Project link</h3>
<h2>2026-08-15 — Documentation: one shared page header, META-driven, with a Project link</h2>

<p><strong>Requested by:</strong> the user liked the header on <code>.md</code> doc pages
(<code>Documentation/MarkdownViewer.tt</code>: title + <em>Current Site</em> + <em>User Role</em> +
<em>Last Updated</em> + <em>Documentation Home</em> + <em>Suggest Edit</em>) and wanted the same on
<code>.tt</code> doc pages — plus a link to the project the documentation belongs to, derived from META.</p>

<h3>What changed</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>New shared include</strong> <code>root/admin/documentation/_doc_header.tt</code> — renders the
        consistent header for <em>both</em> <code>.tt</code> and <code>.md</code> doc pages. All values are
        data-driven from the stash (META block + request context); nothing is hardcoded except labels.</li>
    <li><strong>Project link</strong> — when a doc declares <code>project_id</code> (and optionally
        <code>project_code</code>) in its META (or, for <code>.md</code>, a
        <code>project_id = "NNN"</code> / <code>project_code = "CODE"</code> line), the header shows
        <code>Project: #NNN (CODE)</code> linking to <code>/project/details?project_id=NNN</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Wired into</strong> <code>DocumentationTtTemplate.tt</code> (replacing its hand-rolled
        last-updated line) and <code>MarkdownViewer.tt</code> (replacing its inline header), so every new
        <code>.tt</code> doc gets the header by <code>INCLUDE</code> and existing docs pick it up on next touch.</li>
    <li><strong>Controller wiring</strong> — <code>Documentation.pm</code> now passes
        <code>project_id</code>/<code>project_code</code> (parsed from META) and <code>last_updated</code> into the
        stash for both file types. <code>ScanMethods.pm _extract_md_metadata</code> now parses
        <code>project_id</code>/<code>project_code</code> from <code>.md</code> docs
        (RULE P1 — a plan must be linked to a project).</li>
    <li><strong>Theme compliance</strong> — new <code>.doc-page-header*</code> classes added to
        <code>root/static/css/components/documentation.css</code>; the include uses only
        <code>.doc-*</code> / <code>var(--*)</code> — no inline <code>style=</code>, no hardcoded hex.</li>
    <li><strong>First "touched" files</strong> carrying the linkage:
        <code>DocumentationTtTemplate.tt</code> META → <code>project_id=47</code> (Doc), and
        <code>TodoListPageDisplayTuningPlan.md</code> → <code>project_id=240</code> (TODOLIST-UI).</li>
</ul>

<h3>Verification</h3>
<ul>
    <li>All three templates parse cleanly (Template::Document parse).</li>
    <li>Standalone render of the include with <code>doc_project_id=240</code> outputs
        <code>Project: #240 (TODOLIST-UI)</code> → <code>/project/details?project_id=240</code>.</li>
    <li>Parsers verified on the real files: <code>.md</code> → <code>project_id=240</code>,
        <code>.tt</code> → <code>project_id=47</code>.</li>
    <li>Live admin view: hard-refresh a doc page to confirm the header + Project link render
        (Guest is role-gated by design, so the link is only visible when logged in).</li>
</ul>

<h3>Files</h3>
<ul>
    <li><code>root/admin/documentation/_doc_header.tt</code> (new)</li>
    <li><code>root/Documentation/DocumentationTtTemplate.tt</code></li>
    <li><code>root/Documentation/MarkdownViewer.tt</code></li>
    <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Documentation.pm</code></li>
    <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Documentation/ScanMethods.pm</code></li>
    <li><code>root/static/css/components/documentation.css</code></li>
    <li><code>root/Documentation/TodoListPageDisplayTuningPlan.md</code></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="2026-08-15-git-diff-viewer-shared-widget" class="cl-entry">
<h3>Git diff system — canonical shared widget built (git-diff-viewer.js)</h3>
<div class="container">

    <h1 class="doc-h1">Git diff system — canonical shared widget built</h1>

    <div class="last-updated" doc-muted>
        Last Updated: 2026-08-15 | Version: 1.00 | Author: hermes | Status: Implemented (linked to project #238 GITWT-NEW, todo #1991)
    </div>

    <div id="toc" class="row doc-toc">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">Quick Navigation</h2>
            <div class="doc-navrow">
                <a href="#summary" class="doc-navlink">Summary</a>
                <a href="#why" class="doc-navlink">Why</a>
                <a href="#files" class="doc-navlink">Files Changed</a>
                <a href="#endpoints" class="doc-navlink">Endpoints</a>
                <a href="#verify" class="doc-navlink">Verification</a>
                <a href="#related" class="doc-navlink">Related</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="summary" class="doc-h2">1. Summary</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">The <a href="/Documentation/system/git_worktree_merge_plan" class="doc-link">git_worktree_merge_plan.tt</a> &sect;3.5 decision — exactly ONE diff renderer, reused by every surface — had been documented but never built. Two bespoke inline renderers existed instead (one in <code>git-dashboard.js</code>, one in <code>ai2editor/file-diff.js</code>). This change implements the decision: a real canonical widget <code>root/static/js/git-diff-viewer.js</code> (namespace <code>ComservGitDiff</code>) now owns all diff rendering, and both surfaces were refactored to call it. No second diff renderer remains.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="why" class="doc-h2">2. Why (reconciliation)</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Plan said:</strong> build <code>git-diff-viewer.js</code> with API <code>renderDiff(targetEl, diffText, { scope, editable, onApprove, onReject })</code>; all surfaces consume it; no per-surface renderer.</li>
                <li><strong>Code had:</strong> no <code>git-diff-viewer.js</code>. Instead <code>git-dashboard.js</code> rendered an inline <code>&lt;pre&gt;</code> into <code>#git-file-diff</code> (via <code>GET /admin/git/file_diff</code>), and <code>ai2editor/file-diff.js</code> rendered its own inline <code>&lt;pre&gt;</code> into <code>#git-diff-pane</code> (via <code>GET /ai2/file_diff</code>). Two renderers, two copies of load/error/pre logic.</li>
                <li><strong>Also a doc error:</strong> the 2026-08-13 changelog claimed the widget was "seeded in the AI2 editor <code>git-review.js</code>" — that file never existed. Corrected in place.</li>
                <li><strong>Resolution (Path A — follow the plan):</strong> build the shared widget, route both surfaces through it, keep the two working read-only endpoints, and fix the docs to describe reality.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="files" class="doc-h2">3. Files changed</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>root/static/js/git-diff-viewer.js</code> — <strong>NEW</strong>. Canonical shared renderer. Exposes <code>ComservGitDiff.render(targetEl, diffText, { scope, editable, onApprove, onReject, title, onClose })</code> plus <code>showLoading</code>/<code>showError</code>/<code>showMessage</code> helpers. Unified layout with line numbers, add/remove/hunk tinting, all colours via CSS custom properties (no inline hex). <code>textContent</code> for every line — no HTML injection from diff text.</li>
                <li><code>root/static/css/components/git-diff-viewer.css</code> — <strong>NEW</strong>. Theme-token styles for the widget (pre, line numbers, add/del/hunk tint, load/error/message). Loaded via <code>js_load.tt</code>.</li>
                <li><code>root/static/js/git-dashboard.js</code> — <code>bindFileDiff()</code> now calls <code>ComservGitDiff.showLoading/render/showError</code> into <code>#git-file-diff</code>. Removed the inline <code>&lt;pre&gt;</code>/<code>style.color</code> diff code and the <code>#git-file-diff-content</code> / <code>#git-file-diff-title</code> dependencies (panel container retained; widget fills it).</li>
                <li><code>root/static/js/ai2editor/file-diff.js</code> — <code>renderDiff()</code>/<code>loadDiff()</code> now call <code>ComservGitDiff.render/showLoading/showError</code> into <code>#git-diff-pane</code>. Removed the bespoke inline pre + close-button builder; <code>ensureDiffPane()</code> now uses a <code>.git-diff-pane</code> class instead of hardcoded colors.</li>
                <li><code>root/js_load.tt</code> — added the widget <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> + CSS <code>&lt;link&gt;</code> (both <code>?v=&#91;% cv %&#93;</code>) immediately <em>before</em> <code>git-dashboard.js</code> (on <code>/admin/git</code>) and before <code>ai2editor/file-diff.js</code> (on <code>/ai2/editing_widget_popup</code>), so <code>ComservGitDiff</code> exists when consumers run.</li>
                <li><code>root/Documentation/system/git_worktree_merge_plan.tt</code> — &sect;3.5 retitled "DECIDED &amp; BUILT": names the real widget + API, lists the actual endpoints that feed it, and records that the two bespoke renderers were removed. &sect;7 links here.</li>
                <li><code>root/Documentation/changelog/2026-08-13-git-merge-plan-shared-diff-view.tt</code> — corrected the false <code>git-review.js</code> claim and the &sect;2 decision table; added a cross-link to this entry.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="endpoints" class="doc-h2">4. Endpoints that feed the widget</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">The widget is a pure renderer — it does not care which endpoint supplies the text. As implemented, each surface reuses the read-only endpoint it already had:</p>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>GET /admin/git/file_diff?path=&lt;repo-relative&gt;</code> — admin-gated, path confined to repo root; handles tracked <code>git diff HEAD</code> + untracked <code>git diff --no-index /dev/null</code>. Used by the Git Dashboard working-tree Diff button.</li>
                <li><code>GET /ai2/file_diff?path=&lt;editor path&gt;</code> — editor-role gated. Used by the AI2 editor "Changed Files / Diff" action.</li>
                <li><code>GET /admin/git/review/&lt;branch&gt;</code> — the planned branch-wide review endpoint (still pending build under &sect;3.2/&sect;3.3). When it lands, merge-review will reuse the same widget with no renderer change.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="verify" class="doc-h2">5. Verification</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>node --check root/static/js/git-diff-viewer.js</code> — clean.</li>
                <li><code>node --check root/static/js/git-dashboard.js</code> — clean (no remaining inline diff <code>pre</code>/<code>style.color</code>).</li>
                <li><code>node --check root/static/js/ai2editor/file-diff.js</code> — clean (no remaining inline render builder).</li>
                <li>Confirmed exactly one diff renderer file exists; both the dashboard Diff button and the AI2 editor Diff button route through <code>ComservGitDiff</code>.</li>
                <li>Backend endpoints untouched (working, admin/role-gated) — no controller edits.</li>
                <li>Live browser render not captured this session (auth-gated); verify the two Diff buttons in a browser when an admin session is available. Both static JS files are served directly and templates auto-reload on the running <code>:3001</code> process.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="related" class="doc-h2">6. Related</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><a href="/Documentation/system/git_worktree_merge_plan" class="doc-link">git_worktree_merge_plan.tt</a> (&sect;3.5 DECIDED &amp; BUILT — the owning plan, project #238).</li>
                <li><a href="/Documentation/changelog#2026-08-13-git-merge-plan-shared-diff-view" class="doc-link">2026-08-13 — shared diff view + mandatory human approve</a> (decision record; corrected 2026-08-15).</li>
                <li><a href="/Documentation/changelog#2026-08-15-git-file-diff-no-index-fix" class="doc-link">2026-08-15 — file_diff '--no-index' refused fix</a> (popup showed "Diff failed: Refused" for new files; root-cause fix in Util::Git).</li>
                <li><a href="/project/details?project_id=238" class="doc-link">Project #238 (GITWT-NEW)</a> — tracking todos <a href="/todo/details?record_id=1991" class="doc-link">#1991</a> (diff view+edit), <a href="/todo/details?record_id=1993" class="doc-link">#1993</a> (approve gate), <a href="/todo/details?record_id=1992" class="doc-link">#1992</a> (provenance).</li>
                <li><a href="/Documentation/MASTER_PLAN" class="doc-link">MASTER_PLAN.tt</a> — GITWT-NEW (#238) row links here.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <div class="doc-footer">
                <p>Owning project: <a href="/project/details?project_id=238" class="doc-link">#238 (GITWT-NEW)</a>. Implements the &sect;3.5 decision in <a href="/Documentation/system/git_worktree_merge_plan" class="doc-link">git_worktree_merge_plan.tt</a>. Cross-linked from MASTER_PLAN and the plan's &sect;7.</p>
                <p><em>This documentation is part of the Comserv system.</em></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

</div>
</div>
<div id="2026-08-15-git-file-diff-no-index-fix" class="cl-entry">
<h3>Git file_diff — refused</h3>
<div class="container">

    <h1 class="doc-h1">Git Dashboard Diff &rarr; AI2 editor: path-format + --no-index fixes</h1>

    <div class="last-updated" doc-muted>
        Last Updated: 2026-08-15 | Version: 1.00 | Author: hermes | Status: Fixed (linked to project #238 GITWT-NEW, todo #1991)
    </div>

    <div id="toc" class="row doc-toc">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">Quick Navigation</h2>
            <div class="doc-navrow">
                <a href="#summary" class="doc-navlink">Summary</a>
                <a href="#root" class="doc-navlink">Root cause</a>
                <a href="#fix" class="doc-navlink">Fix</a>
                <a href="#files" class="doc-navlink">Files</a>
                <a href="#verify" class="doc-navlink">Verification</a>
                <a href="#related" class="doc-navlink">Related</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="summary" class="doc-h2">1. Summary</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Three coordinated fixes to the Git Dashboard per-file Diff flow. (1) The backend read-only diff endpoint refused its own <code>--no-index</code> flag for new/untracked files (allow-list gap in Util::Git). (2) The inline diff panel showed nothing, so the Diff button was re-routed to open the file in the AI2 editor (<code>/ai2/editing_widget_popup?file=&lt;path&gt;</code>), which is itself a widget consumer and auto-shows that file's diff on open. (3) <strong>The real "no file / empty diff" cause:</strong> <code>git status</code> runs from the repo root so it returns <strong>repo-relative</strong> paths (<code>Comserv/root/...</code>), but the AI2 editor and <code>/ai2/file_diff</code> expect <strong>app-relative</strong> paths (<code>root/...</code>). The dashboard was handing the editor <code>Comserv/root/...</code>, which <code>EditorFile</code> could not resolve (Not found) and the diff mapped to a non-existent path. The dashboard now strips the leading <code>Comserv/</code> segment before opening the editor.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="root" class="doc-h2">2. Root cause</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Path-format mismatch (the "no file / empty diff" cause).</strong> <code>Comserv::Util::Git::_run</code> runs <code>git -C $repo</code> where <code>$repo</code> is the <em>repo root</em> (<code>comserv2/</code>, the parent of <code>Comserv/</code>). So <code>git status --porcelain</code> returns paths relative to the repo root, i.e. <code>Comserv/root/admin/git/index.tt</code> (with the <code>Comserv/</code> prefix). But the AI2 editor's <code>EditorFile-&gt;read_file</code> and <code>/ai2/file_diff</code> resolve paths relative to the <em>app root</em> (<code>Comserv/</code>), so they need <code>root/admin/git/index.tt</code> (no <code>Comserv/</code>). The dashboard was passing the repo-relative <code>Comserv/root/...</code> straight to the editor, so the file load returned Not found and the diff mapped to a non-existent file. This is why the editor opened but showed nothing.</li>
                <li><strong>--no-index flag refusal (only affected new/untracked files).</strong> For untracked files both <code>file_diff</code> endpoints call <code>git diff --no-index /dev/null &lt;file&gt;</code>, but <code>Util::Git::_run</code>'s per-subcommand flag allow-list for <code>diff</code> omitted <code>--no-index</code>, so it was refused before git ran. Tracked files (<code>git diff HEAD</code>) were unaffected by this part.</li>
                <li><strong>Note on an earlier wrong turn:</strong> a first attempt "fixed" <code>file_diff</code> by removing <code>_ai2_repo_rel_path</code>; that mapping is actually correct for app-relative input and was reverted. The genuine fix is the dashboard stripping the <code>Comserv/</code> prefix so the editor receives app-relative paths.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="fix" class="doc-h2">3. Fix</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>lib/Comserv/Util/Git.pm</code> — added <code>--no-index</code> to the <code>diff</code> flag allow-list. This is a read-only comparison flag (no repo mutation), so it is safe to permit. One change fixes <strong>both</strong> endpoints because they share <code>_run</code>.</li>
                <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Admin/Git.pm</code> — added a <code>log_with_details(..., 'warn', 'file_diff', ...)</code> on the diff-failure branch so future diff failures (refusals, git errors, empty output) are recorded in the audit log instead of being silent. <strong>Logging answer:</strong> yes — the app uses <code>Comserv::Util::Logging-&gt;log_with_details</code> everywhere (per .ai-policy.md); the <code>file_diff</code> path simply never logged its failures until now.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="files" class="doc-h2">4. Files changed</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>lib/Comserv/Util/Git.pm</code> — <code>%ALLOWED_FLAGS</code> for <code>diff</code> now includes <code>--no-index</code>.</li>
                <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Admin/Git.pm</code> — <code>file_diff</code> logs failures via <code>log_with_details</code>.</li>
                <li><code>root/static/js/git-dashboard.js</code> — the working-tree <em>Diff</em> button now opens <code>/ai2/editing_widget_popup?file=&lt;path&gt;</code> (a separate window) instead of rendering into the inline <code>#git-file-diff</code> panel. Before opening, it strips the leading <code>Comserv/</code> from the repo-relative git-status path so the editor receives an app-relative path (<code>root/...</code>).</li>
                <li><code>root/ai2/editor/editing_widget_popup.tt</code> — exposes <code>window.AI2_FILE_TO_LOAD</code> when opened with <code>?file=</code>.</li>
                <li><code>root/static/js/ai2editor/file-diff.js</code> — on open with a <code>?file=</code> target, auto-fetches <code>GET /ai2/file_diff</code> and renders it through <code>ComservGitDiff</code> (no extra click).</li>
                <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/AI2.pm</code> — <code>file_diff</code> reverted to using <code>_ai2_repo_rel_path</code> (correct for app-relative input). No change needed there once the dashboard supplies app-relative paths. <code>use File::Spec</code> added (previously missing import). <strong>Correction (2026-08-18):</strong> a follow-up audit todo showed the real <code>ai2/file_diff</code> bug was a doubled path (<code>Comserv/../Comserv/Comserv/...</code>) from <code>catfile($app_dir, $raw)</code>; it was NOT fully fixed here. See <a href="/Documentation/changelog#2026-08-18-ai2-file-diff-doubled-path" class="doc-link">2026-08-18 AI2 file_diff doubled-path fix</a>.</li>
                <li>No separate per-surface diff renderer created — the editor remains the sole widget consumer for this flow.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="verify" class="doc-h2">5. Verification</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>perl -Ilib -c lib/Comserv/Util/Git.pm</code> — syntax OK.</li>
                <li><code>perl -Ilib -c lib/Comserv/Controller/Admin/Git.pm</code> — syntax OK.</li>
                <li><code>perl -Ilib -c lib/Comserv/Controller/AI2.pm</code> — syntax OK (shares the fix via <code>_run</code>).</li>
                <li>Both endpoints auto-reload on the running <code>:3001</code> process (no server restart, per ops rule). Re-test by clicking Diff on an <strong>untracked/new</strong> file — it should now show the full new content as additions, and on a modified file show the vs-HEAD diff.</li>
                <li>If a diff still fails, the audit log now carries a <code>file_diff</code> warn entry with the path, is_new flag, git error, and exit code — check the log for the exact cause.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="related" class="doc-h2">6. Related</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><a href="/Documentation/changelog#2026-08-15-git-diff-viewer-shared-widget" class="doc-link">2026-08-15 — shared diff widget built</a> (the widget this popup now uses).</li>
                <li><a href="/Documentation/system/git_worktree_merge_plan" class="doc-link">git_worktree_merge_plan.tt</a> &sect;3.5 (project #238).</li>
                <li><a href="/project/details?project_id=238" class="doc-link">Project #238 (GITWT-NEW)</a>, <a href="/todo/details?record_id=1991" class="doc-link">todo #1991</a>.</li>
                <li><a href="/Documentation/MASTER_PLAN" class="doc-link">MASTER_PLAN.tt</a>.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <div class="doc-footer">
                <p>Owning project: <a href="/project/details?project_id=238" class="doc-link">#238 (GITWT-NEW)</a>. Bug fix to the read-only diff endpoint; widget unchanged. Cross-linked from MASTER_PLAN.</p>
                <p><em>This documentation is part of the Comserv system.</em></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

</div>
</div>
<div id="2026-08-16-ai2-project-tab-file-tree" class="cl-entry">
<h3>AI2 editor Project tab: full project file tree + changed files at top</h3>
<div class="container">

    <h1 class="doc-h1">AI2 editor Project tab — full file tree + changed files on top</h1>

    <div class="last-updated" doc-muted>
        Last Updated: 2026-08-16 | Version: 1.00 | Author: hermes | Status: Implemented (linked to project #238 GITWT-NEW)
    </div>

    <div id="toc" class="row doc-toc">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">Quick Navigation</h2>
            <div class="doc-navrow">
                <a href="#summary" class="doc-navlink">Summary</a>
                <a href="#behaviour" class="doc-navlink">Behaviour</a>
                <a href="#files" class="doc-navlink">Files</a>
                <a href="#verify" class="doc-navlink">Verification</a>
                <a href="#related" class="doc-navlink">Related</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="summary" class="doc-h2">1. Summary</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">The AI2 code-editor "Project" sidebar panel previously showed only a hardcoded two-file placeholder (<code>AI2.pm</code>, <code>editing_widget_popup.tt</code>) plus a live "CHANGED FILES" list. It now renders the <strong>entire project file tree</strong> (folders collapsible, with a filter box), and pins a live <strong>CHANGED FILES</strong> section at the top so uncommitted work is always visible first. Each file row is clickable to open it for editing; each row also carries a <strong>Diff</strong> button that opens the file's working-tree diff in the shared <code>#git-diff-pane</code> (same widget the rest of the app uses). Changed files get an <code>M</code> (modified) or <code>U</code> (new/untracked) badge.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="behaviour" class="doc-h2">2. Behaviour</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Changed files pinned at top.</strong> A <code>GET /ai2/git_status</code> call populates a "CHANGED FILES (N)" header, each row with an <code>M</code>/<code>U</code> badge, a name, and a <strong>Diff</strong> button.</li>
                <li><strong>Full tree below.</strong> A <code>GET /ai2/file_tree</code> call renders the whole project as a nested, collapsible tree (dirs first, then files), rooted at the app dir. A filter box above the tree narrows by full path or base name (empty folders are hidden under a filter).</li>
                <li><strong>Click a file → edit.</strong> Clicking any file row loads it into the Ace editor via the new <code>AI2EditorCore.openFile(path)</code> (reuses <code>/ai2/load_file</code>, resets dirty/save state, updates the tab label + status, and tells the chat sidebar the active file).</li>
                <li><strong>Click Diff → diff.</strong> The <strong>Diff</strong> button (with <code>stopPropagation</code> so it does not also open the file) fetches <code>GET /ai2/file_diff</code> and renders through <code>ComservGitDiff</code> into <code>#git-diff-pane</code>. It reuses <code>ai2editor/file-diff.js</code>'s loader, so the two never clobber the AI-suggestion <code>#ai-diff-pane</code>.</li>
                <li><strong>Badges in the tree.</strong> Tree file rows that also appear in the git-status change-set get the same <code>M</code>/<code>U</code> badge + Diff button, so the whole tree is aware of uncommitted work.</li>
                <li><strong>Diff only on git-changed files.</strong> The <strong>Diff</strong> button is rendered only when git lists the file as changed (M/U). Clean files get no Diff affordance, so the UI never implies a phantom diff on an unchanged file. This is driven entirely by <code>git status --porcelain</code> — if git doesn't flag it, no Diff button.</li>
                <li><strong>Folders start collapsed.</strong> The full tree renders every directory collapsed (▸); click a folder to expand. The filter box narrows by path/base name and hides empty folders.</li>
                <li><strong>Editor re-layouts on resize.</strong> Opening the Project panel or resizing the window/panel now triggers <code>Ace.resize()</code> so the editor content always fills the available area (new <code>AI2EditorCore.resizeEditor</code>, wired to <code>ai2:panel-open</code>/<code>ai2:panel-close</code>/<code>ai2:panel-resize</code> and <code>window.resize</code>).</li>
                <li><strong>Left sidebar is resizable.</strong> The Project/Git/etc. panel container now has a right-edge drag handle (160–600px), so it is no longer fixed-width.</li>
                <li><strong>Bug fix — file_diff "Could not access" on repo-root / app-dir mismatch.</strong> <code>_ai2_repo_rel_path</code> previously assumed the git repo root was one level above the app dir, so when <code>repo_path()</code> resolves the repo to the app dir (<code>Comserv/</code>) while the real <code>.git</code> is at <code>comserv2/</code>, diff paths were rebuilt relative to the wrong root and produced malformed paths like <code>Comserv/Comserv/script/...</code> ("Could not access"). Now it resolves the TRUE toplevel via <code>git rev-parse --show-toplevel</code>, strips it (plus the leading <code>Comserv/</code> app-dir segment, since git resolves relative diff paths against the toplevel), and determines new-vs-tracked via <code>git ls-files --error-unmatch</code> (read-only, added to the Util::Git whitelist) instead of a wrong-base <code>-e</code> check. Files at the repo root (e.g. <code>docker-compose.prod.yml</code>) now diff correctly.</li>
                <li><strong>Layout fix — side panels locked to window edges (no overlap).</strong> The left Project/Git/etc. panel and the right chat sidebar are now proper flex children of <code>.main</code> (the earlier absolute-positioned left panel that floated over and covered the editor is gone). Opening the left panel pushes the editor right; closing it (or hiding the chat) lets the editor expand to fill the freed space — both panels stay pinned to the window edges. The left panel remains drag-resizable (160–600px) and the chat remains resizable.</li>
                <li><strong>UI improvement — diff sits BESIDE the editor (right rail).</strong> The editor area is now a horizontal flex row: code on the left, a right-hand rail (42% width, min 260px) holding the diff panes. The git diff (and the AI suggestion) now render beside the code rather than stacked below it, so you compare them side-by-side without scrolling. The git-diff pane fills the rail height and keeps its Unified/Split toggle.</li>
                <li><strong>Chat detach hardened.</strong> The detach/attach toggle and the detached-window construction are now wrapped in try/catch with guarded <code>window.opener</code> access and no aggressive <code>setInterval</code> watchers, so a blocked popup or opener error can no longer crash the editor window. Close (✕) + floating 💬 reopen + detach (⤢) all share one view-state function; closing the detached window re-attaches cleanly without forcing the chat open if it was also closed.</li>
                <li><strong>Diff correctness — deployment-agnostic path resolution (final fix).</strong> The remaining "shows as new" bug was traced to <code>_ai2_repo_rel_path</code> computing the git prefix via <code>git rev-parse --show-prefix</code> run from <code>repo_path()</code> (the repo root), where that prefix is <code>""</code> — so the returned pathspec lost the <code>Comserv/</code> segment and <code>git diff HEAD</code> matched nothing (→ <code>is_new=1</code> → "new file"). Replaced with <code>File::Spec::abs2rel($app_dir, $repo_root)</code> (the relative path from the repo root down to wherever the code actually runs), joined with the app-relative path. This is exact, deterministic, deployment-agnostic, and never depends on git's cwd or a hardcoded string. Verified via a direct invocation of the controller logic: <code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Admin/Docker.pm</code> now resolves to <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Controller/Admin/Docker.pm</code>, <code>is_new=0</code>, and a real 132-line modification diff. <strong>U = untracked</strong> (never committed); <strong>M = modified</strong> (tracked file changed vs HEAD).</li>
                <li><strong>Title-bar Diff button + scroll-lock.</strong> The editor title bar now has a <strong>Diff</strong> button that shows the currently-open file's git diff in the right rail (same as clicking a tree/file Diff). Scrolling the code and the diff now stay in lock-step (proportional scroll-sync, guarded against feedback loops) so the same lines remain visible in both.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="files" class="doc-h2">3. Files changed</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/AI2.pm</code> — new <code>file_tree :Local</code> action: editor/admin/developer-gated, pure <code>readdir</code> recursion (no shell, no chdir), path-confined to the app root, skips <code>.git</code>/<code>node_modules</code>/<code>blib</code>/<code>.hermes</code>/<code>logs</code>/<code>tmp</code>/vendor dirs and <code>.bak</code>/<code>.swp</code>/<code>.tmp</code> files. Returns <code>{ success, root, tree }</code> where <code>tree</code> is a nested <code>{ type, name, path, children? }</code> structure.</li>
                <li><code>root/static/js/ai2editor/core.js</code> — new <code>AI2EditorCore.openFile(path)</code>: on-demand loader that sets the Ace value, resets dirty/save state, updates tab label/status, and notifies the chat/popup of the active file. Safe to call before Ace is ready (brief poll). Also new <code>AI2EditorCore.resizeEditor()</code> (guarded so it never creates a stray empty editor) wired to <code>window.resize</code> + <code>ai2:panel-open/close/resize</code> events.</li>
                <li><code>root/static/js/ai2editor/sidebar-toggle.js</code> — new <code>wireResize()</code>: adds a right-edge drag handle to the <code>#sidebar-panels</code> container (160–600px) so the left panel is resizable; dispatches <code>ai2:panel-resize</code> and <code>ai2:panel-close</code> events.</li>
                <li><code>root/static/js/ai2editor/project-tree.js</code> — Diff button rendered ONLY for git-changed files (M/U); directories render collapsed by default; filter box hides empty folders.</li>
                <li><code>root/ai2/editor/editing_widget_popup.tt</code> — removed the hardcoded 2-file <code>ul.file-tree</code> placeholder from <code>#panel-projects</code>; kept the <code>#ai2-changed-files</code> host (module injects the filter + tree itself).</li>
                <li><code>root/js_load.tt</code> — loads <code>ai2editor/project-tree.js</code> (defer) on the <code>/ai2/editing_widget_popup</code> route, after core.js + the shared diff widget + file-diff.js.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
