<h2>2026-08-13 — /planning/daily rebuilt as a clean index (replaced the broken monolith)</h2>

<p><strong>Decision:</strong> After multiple failed attempts to patch the floating buttons
(AI Editor / Back-to-Top / Chat) on the old <code>/planning/daily</code> monolith, the page
was rebuilt from scratch per the owner's direction. The old monolith trapped the global
<code>position:fixed</code> floating buttons inside its nested tab content (full-page
<code>?tab=</code> fetches were injected via <code>innerHTML</code>), making the buttons
unreachable. Patching CSS/JS on top of that structure was whack-a-mole.</p>

<p><strong>New structure:</strong></p>
<ul>
    <li><code>/planning/daily</code> is now a <strong>clean index page</strong> (<code>admin/planning/DailyPlan.tt</code>) with three <strong>hard-coded links</strong>: <strong>Daily Priorities</strong>, <strong>Master Plan</strong>, <strong>Calendar</strong>. It is a normal page, so the global floating buttons (Back-to-Top / AI Editor / Chat from <code>layout.tt</code>/<code>js_load.tt</code>) render correctly — the nested full-page injection that broke them is gone.</li>
    <li><strong>Daily Priorities</strong> → new route <code>/planning/daily-priorities/&lt;date&gt;</code> (<code>Planning.pm sub daily_priorities</code>) renders <code>admin/planning/DailyPriorities.tt</code>, which INCLUDEs the existing <code>_today_work_tab.tt</code> (Start Day / End Day / Triage / Reschedule / Today's Log action bar, focus queue, remaining-todos). Verified: action bar + focus queue render.</li>
    <li><strong>Calendar</strong> → links to <code>/todo/day/&lt;date&gt;</code>, the existing gcal <strong>day calendar</strong> view (the real day-grid, not a todo list).</li>
    <li><strong>Master Plan</strong> → links to <code>/Documentation/MASTER_PLAN</code> (unchanged, working).</li>
    <li><strong>Old monolith preserved</strong> as <code>admin/planning/DailyPlan.legacy.tt</code>, served read-only at <code>/planning/daily-legacy</code> (new <code>legacy_daily</code> action → refactored <code>daily_impl</code> private method). Kept for reference; does NOT carry live data when opened standalone and is intended to be re-integrated later as a tab on the main page.</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Verified:</strong></p>
<ul>
    <li><code>perl -Ilib -c lib/Comserv/Controller/Planning.pm</code> &rarr; syntax OK.</li>
    <li>Rendered <code>DailyPlan.tt</code> (index) and <code>DailyPriorities.tt</code> through the app's Template Toolkit: index emits all three hard-coded links; Daily Priorities emits the action bar (Start Day / End Day / Triage / Reschedule / Today's Log) and focus-queue section.</li>
    <li>Routes present: <code>daily</code> (<code>/planning/daily</code>), <code>daily_priorities</code> (<code>/planning/daily-priorities</code>), <code>legacy_daily</code> (<code>/planning/daily-legacy</code>); <code>daily_log</code> untouched.</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Files touched:</strong></p>
<ul>
    <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Planning.pm</code> — <code>daily</code> now renders the clean index; added <code>daily_priorities</code> + <code>legacy_daily</code> + private <code>daily_impl</code>.</li>
    <li><code>root/admin/planning/DailyPlan.tt</code> — rewritten as the clean index (was the monolith; old version moved to <code>DailyPlan.legacy.tt</code>).</li>
    <li><code>root/admin/planning/DailyPriorities.tt</code> — new focused Daily Priorities page.</li>
    <li><code>root/static/css/planning/daily-plan.css</code> — added <code>.daily-index*</code> card styles (theme-token driven, no fixed geometry).</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Next steps (add one feature at a time):</strong> re-introduce the week / month / gantt / resources views as their own routes or lazy-loaded fragments; eventually re-surface the legacy monolith as a tab on the main index.</p>

<h2>2026-08-13 — Removed duplicate action bar on /planning/daily; added End Day + Open Logs</h2>

<p><code>/planning/daily</code> rendered two identical action bars: a top-level "Day Controls" card above the tab bar and a second one inside the Daily Priorities tab. The second (in-tab) bar was the duplicate and is now hidden on this page via <code>hide_action_bar = 1</code> on the <code>_today_work_tab.tt</code> include; the top card stays as the only action bar. <strong>End Day</strong> and <strong>Open Logs</strong> were added to that card and are now always visible (previously Start Day / Open Logs / End Day were mutually exclusive based on log state). No other buttons changed. The shared inner bar still shows on DailyPriorities and DailyPlan.legacy. See <a href="/Documentation/changelog#2026-08-13-daily-plan-remove-duplicate-action-card">the full note</a>.</p>



<div id="2026-08-17-git-dashboard-git-branch-rename" class="cl-entry">
    <h2>2026-08-17 — Git Dashboard: rename `git` worktree branch to `git-dev` to unblock merges</h2>
    <p><strong>Last Updated:</strong> 2026-08-17 | <strong>Version:</strong> 1.00 | <strong>Author:</strong> hermes | <strong>Status:</strong> Fixed (linked to project #238 GITWT-NEW)</p>

    <h3>Problem</h3>
    <p>The zenflow worktree at <code>~/.comserv/worktrees/git/Comserv</code> tracked a branch literally named <code>git</code>. That name collides with the <code>git</code> command itself, so <code>git checkout git</code> / <code>git switch git</code> are ambiguous and <strong>merges of that branch fail</strong> (the dashboard reported "Failed to switch to or create branch 'git'"). The Git Dashboard offered the <code>git</code> branch in its Switch dropdown and validated it as "known", then died on checkout.</p>

    <h3>Fix</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Branch renamed</strong> <code>git</code> &rarr; <code>git-dev</code> from inside the worktree (<code>git branch -m git git-dev</code>), preserving its 1 unique commit (<code>67cbb177</code>). The worktree now tracks <code>git-dev</code>; no code/commits lost.</li>
        <li><strong><code>Comserv/Util/Git.pm</code> &rarr; <code>get_local_branches</code></strong>: skip a branch literally named <code>git</code> (reserved word). This removes it from the dashboard dropdown <em>and</em> from the validation hash used by the switch/delete handlers — defense in depth against any future <code>git</code>-named branch.</li>
        <li><strong><code>Comserv/Controller/Admin/Git.pm</code> &rarr; <code>op=switch</code></strong>: explicitly reject <code>branch=git</code> with a clear "reserved" message (also protects <code>op=delbranch</code>, which shares the same validation).</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Why not just add a rename button</h3>
    <p>A dashboard "rename branch" feature does not exist yet (confirmed: no endpoint, no UI). The <code>git</code>&rarr;<code>git-dev</code> rename was done at the shell to unblock work immediately. A first-class Rename-branch control is now on the backlog — see <a href="/Documentation/plans/2026-08-17-git-dashboard-merge-ui" class="doc-link">git-dashboard-merge-ui plan, &sect;7.1</a> (project GITWT-NEW #238).</p>

    <h3>Verified</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Both controllers compile: <code>perl -Ilib -c</code> &rarr; syntax OK.</li>
        <li><code>admin/git/index.tt</code> renders clean (TT cache disabled): RENDER OK, exit 0.</li>
        <li><code>git-dev</code> present in <code>get_local_branches</code> output; literal <code>git</code> excluded (verified against real repo).</li>
        <li>Worktree reports <code>[git-dev]</code>; <code>git rev-list --left-right --count main...git-dev</code> &rarr; <code>1 0</code> (1 commit ahead, 0 behind).</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Files touched</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><code>lib/Comserv/Util/Git.pm</code> — <code>get_local_branches</code> skips reserved <code>git</code> branch.</li>
        <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Admin/Git.pm</code> — <code>op=switch</code> rejects <code>branch=git</code>.</li>
        <li><code>root/Documentation/plans/2026-08-17-git-dashboard-merge-ui.md</code> — &sect;7.1 backlog (rename-branch feature), &sect;8 status.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>See also</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="/Documentation/plans/2026-08-17-git-dashboard-merge-ui" class="doc-link">2026-08-17 Git Dashboard Merge UI plan</a> — the merge feature (main&rarr;branch, branch&rarr;main) still to be built into the dashboard; the <code>git</code>&rarr;<code>git-dev</code> rename unblocks it.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div id="2026-08-17-git-dashboard-merge-ui" class="cl-entry">
    <h2>2026-08-17 — Git Dashboard: Merge UI (main &rarr; branch, branch &rarr; main, one at a time)</h2>
    <p><strong>Last Updated:</strong> 2026-08-17 | <strong>Version:</strong> 1.00 | <strong>Author:</strong> hermes | <strong>Status:</strong> Shipped (linked to project #238 GITWT-NEW)</p>

    <h3>Problem</h3>
    <p>The Git Dashboard had no way to merge <code>main</code> into a selected branch (or a branch into <code>main</code>) from the browser — PyCharm-equivalent one-at-a-time merges had to be done by hand. Two blocking bugs were found and fixed in the process:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>"Already up to date" lie (wrong merge source).</strong> The merge action merged <code>origin/main</code> rather than the local <code>main</code> ref. When local <code>main</code> had unpushed commits, <code>origin/main</code> was stale and <code>git merge origin/main</code> reported "Already up to date" even though <code>main</code>'s code was never delivered to the branch.</li>
        <li><strong>Vanishing result (wiped on success).</strong> The JS handler called <code>location.reload()</code> / <code>refreshGitDashboard()</code> on success, which re-rendered the Merge card and wiped the status + <code>&lt;pre&gt;</code> output before the user could read it — the result "disappeared almost instantly."</li>
        <li><strong>Worktree path resolution.</strong> <code>git worktree list --porcelain</code> drops the <code>worktree &lt;path&gt;</code> line for the <code>git-dev</code> worktree (stale metadata from the <code>git</code>&rarr;<code>git-dev</code> rename), so <code>worktree_checkout_path_for_branch</code> returned <code>undef</code> &rarr; "not checked out in any worktree."</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Fix</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong><code>Controller::Admin::Git::merge</code> (POST /admin/git/merge)</strong> now merges the <strong>local <code>main</code></strong> ref (the code visible on the dashboard), not <code>origin/main</code>, for both the main&rarr;branch and branch&rarr;main worktree-sync paths. Both directions run <em>inside the branch's own worktree checkout</em> via <code>_run(..., { repo =&gt; $wt_path })</code>; a worktree branch is already checked out so it is never switched in the main repo (git refuses "already used by worktree").</li>
        <li><strong><code>Util::Git::worktree_checkout_path_for_branch</code></strong>: added a directory scan of the worktree base dir (<code>~/.comserv/worktrees/*/Comserv</code>) that matches each checkout's actual branch via <code>git branch --show-current</code>, bypassing the corrupt porcelain. Fixed the scan to test <code>-e</code> (exists) not <code>-d</code> — a worktree's <code>.git</code> is a <em>file</em> (gitdir pointer), not a directory.</li>
        <li><strong><code>root/static/js/git-dashboard.js</code></strong>: removed the auto-refresh/reload on merge success so the status badge + output <code>&lt;pre&gt;</code> stay visible until a manual hard-refresh. Added <code>console.log('[git-dashboard] merge response:', res)</code> so the full server response (incl. any error line) is captured in DevTools even if the DOM flashes.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>How it works</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Merge main &rarr; branch</strong> (source=main, target=branch): <code>fetch origin</code> then <code>git -C &lt;worktree&gt; merge --no-ff main</code>. No test gate (updating a worktree, not main).</li>
        <li><strong>Merge branch &rarr; main</strong> (source=branch, target=main): <code>run_test_gate</code> blocks on red; optional best-effort sync of the branch's worktree to main; then <code>merge_branch($c, $source)</code> in the main repo.</li>
        <li><strong>Conflict</strong> &rarr; <code>{ conflict=&gt;1, output }</code>; the UI reveals a one-click <strong>Abort</strong> (POST /admin/git/merge/abort &rarr; <code>git merge --abort</code>).</li>
        <li>All git via <code>git_service</code> (<code>_run</code> whitelist); logged via <code>log_with_details</code>. Admin-gated <code>git_merge</code>; reserved <code>git</code> branch rejected.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Verified</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Both modules compile: <code>perl -Ilib -c</code> &rarr; syntax OK.</li>
        <li><code>admin/git/index.tt</code> renders clean (TT cache disabled): RENDER OK.</li>
        <li><code>node --check root/static/js/git-dashboard.js</code> &rarr; OK.</li>
        <li>Dry run on the real <code>git-dev</code> worktree: <code>git -C ~/.comserv/worktrees/git/Comserv merge --no-ff --no-commit main</code> &rarr; "Automatic merge went well" bringing in the 4 local-main commits (previously "Already up to date" because it targeted stale <code>origin/main</code>); <code>--abort</code> cleaned up non-destructively.</li>
        <li><strong>Live:</strong> on <code>/admin/git</code> (port 3001), selecting <code>git-dev</code> &rarr; "Merge main &rarr; this branch" reports <strong>merged</strong> with the commit output staying visible, and the <code>git-dev</code> worktree now carries <code>main</code>'s code (Merge tab, branch-visibility fixes).</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Files touched</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Admin/Git.pm</code> — <code>merge</code> action: merge local <code>main</code> (not <code>origin/main</code>); <code>merge_abort</code> action already present.</li>
        <li><code>lib/Comserv/Util/Git.pm</code> — <code>worktree_checkout_path_for_branch</code>: directory-scan resolution by actual branch (<code>-e</code> not <code>-d</code>).</li>
        <li><code>root/static/js/git-dashboard.js</code> — sticky merge result (no auto-reload); console capture of response.</li>
        <li><code>root/admin/git/index.tt</code> — Merge <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> card (built in prior work).</li>
        <li><code>root/Documentation/plans/2026-08-17-git-dashboard-merge-ui.md</code> &mdash; &sect;3 direction logic corrected (worktree-internal merge), &sect;8 status updated to Shipped.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>See also</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="/Documentation/plans/2026-08-17-git-dashboard-merge-ui" class="doc-link">2026-08-17 Git Dashboard Merge UI plan</a> &mdash; &sect;7.1 backlog: first-class "Rename branch" control (the <code>git</code>&rarr;<code>git-dev</code> rename was done at the shell for now).</li>
        <li><a href="/Documentation/changelog/CHANGELOG#2026-08-17-git-dashboard-git-branch-rename" class="doc-link">2026-08-17 Git Dashboard branch rename</a> &mdash; the rename that unblocked this feature.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div id="2026-08-18-logging-mysql-reconnect-retry" class="cl-entry">
<h3>Admin::Logging index &mdash; MySQL transient-connection retry</h3>
<div class="container">

    <h1 class="doc-h1">Logging admin: self-heal "Lost connection to MySQL server during query"</h1>

    <div class="last-updated" doc-muted>
        Last Updated: 2026-08-18 | Version: 1.00 | Author: hermes | Status: Fixed
    </div>

    <div id="toc" class="row doc-toc">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">Quick Navigation</h2>
            <div class="doc-navrow">
                <a href="#summary" class="doc-navlink">Summary</a>
                <a href="#root" class="doc-navlink">Root cause</a>
                <a href="#fix" class="doc-navlink">Fix</a>
                <a href="#files" class="doc-navlink">Files</a>
                <a href="#verify" class="doc-navlink">Verification</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="summary" class="doc-h2">1. Summary</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">The Application Error Audit todo <code>admin/logging &mdash; Failed to fetch system_log records: DBIx::Class ... Lost connection to MySQL server during query</code> (logged 2026-08-17) is now fixed. A sub-second DB connection drop during the <code>system_log</code> fetch no longer re-raises the error and opens a spurious audit todo.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="root" class="doc-h2">2. Root cause</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li>The connection config (<code>Model/DBEncy.pm</code>) sets <code>mariadb_auto_reconnect =&gt; 1</code>, but DBD::MariaDB only repairs the <em>next</em> statement after a drop &mdash; it does <strong>not</strong> retry the in-flight query that already failed. So a "Lost connection during query" raised from the cached (now-dead) handle.</li>
                <li>The Logging <code>index</code> retry block only fell back for a missing <code>system_identifier</code> column; it reused the same cached handle, so a transient drop still failed and re-logged the very error in the todo.</li>
                <li>Same-day commit <code>67cbb177</code> hardened <code>Admin::HardwareMonitor</code> with a disconnect+reconnect-once pattern for exactly this class of error, but the Logging <code>index</code> path was missed.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="fix" class="doc-h2">3. Fix</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Admin/Logging.pm</code> &mdash; added <code>$attempt_with_reconnect</code>: on a connection-drop error (<code>Lost connection</code> / <code>server has gone away</code> / <code>MySQL server</code>) it disconnects, grabs a fresh handle via <code>$schema-&gt;storage-&gt;dbh</code>, and retries the whole fetch <strong>once</strong>. Mirrors the proven <code>Admin::HardwareMonitor</code> pattern.</li>
                <li>The guard wraps both the full-column fetch and the base-column fallback, and the area-counts query. Only if the retry also fails does it fall through to logging the error (so genuine failures still surface).</li>
                <li>Extracted an <code>$area_counts_stash</code> helper so the grouped breakdown is populated in both the primary and retry paths.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="files" class="doc-h2">4. Files changed</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Admin/Logging.pm</code> &mdash; <code>index</code>: transient-connection reconnect guard (uncommitted, pending commit).</li>
                <li>Unchanged: <code>lib/Comserv/Model/DBEncy.pm</code> (auto-reconnect attr already present); <code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Admin/HardwareMonitor.pm</code> (already hardened in <code>67cbb177</code>).</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="verify" class="doc-h2">5. Verification</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>perl -Ilib -c lib/Comserv/Controller/Admin/Logging.pm</code> &rarr; syntax OK.</li>
                <li>Standalone <code>:3001</code> auto-reloads the <code>.pm</code>, so the guard is live on the next request (no restart).</li>
                <li>A sub-second blip now self-heals within the request; a genuine outage still surfaces the error after the single retry.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

</div>
</div>

<div id="2026-08-18-ai2-file-diff-doubled-path" class="cl-entry">
<h3>AI2 /ai2/file_diff &mdash; doubled-path fix</h3>
<div class="container">

    <h1 class="doc-h1">AI2 editor diff: real doubled-path bug fixed (Comserv/../Comserv/Comserv/...)</h1>

    <div class="last-updated" doc-muted>
        Last Updated: 2026-08-18 | Version: 1.00 | Author: hermes | Status: Fixed
    </div>

    <div id="toc" class="row doc-toc">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">Quick Navigation</h2>
            <div class="doc-navrow">
                <a href="#summary" class="doc-navlink">Summary</a>
                <a href="#root" class="doc-navlink">Root cause</a>
                <a href="#fix" class="doc-navlink">Fix</a>
                <a href="#files" class="doc-navlink">Files</a>
                <a href="#verify" class="doc-navlink">Verification</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="summary" class="doc-h2">1. Summary</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">The Application Error Audit todo <code>ai2/file_diff &mdash; git diff --no-index /dev/null .../Comserv/../home/.../Comserv/Comserv/docker-compose.prod.yml</code> (logged 2026-08-16) is now fixed. The error was a <strong>real, reproducible bug</strong> &mdash; not a transient artifact.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="root" class="doc-h2">2. Root cause</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>AI2.pm file_diff</code> built the on-disk path as <code>File::Spec-&gt;catfile($app_dir, $raw_frontend_path)</code>. The frontend sends an <em>app-relative</em> editor path, but it can already carry the repo/app dir prefix (or be absolute). When it does, the concatenation double-appends the directory, producing the exact bogus path in the log: <code>Comserv/..//home/shanta/PycharmProjects/comserv2/Comserv/Comserv/docker-compose.prod.yml</code>.</li>
                <li>That path does not exist, so <code>git diff --no-index /dev/null &lt;nonexistent&gt;</code> exits 1 with no output. <code>Util::Git::git_run</code> logs every non-zero exit as ERROR (no benign-exception rule covers a missing <code>--no-index</code> target), which is what opened the audit todo.</li>
                <li>Note: the 2026-08-15 changelog entry <em>"Git file_diff &mdash; refused"</em> asserted "no change needed in AI2.pm" &mdash; that was incorrect; the doubled-path defect was still present and is the actual root cause of this todo.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="fix" class="doc-h2">3. Fix</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/AI2.pm</code> &mdash; <code>file_diff</code> now derives the on-disk path as <code>&lt;repo_root&gt;/&lt;repo_rel&gt;</code>: it joins the resolved git repo root with the <em>already-correct</em> <code>repo_rel</code> returned by <code>_ai2_repo_rel_path</code> (the same value <code>git ls-files</code>/<code>git diff HEAD</code> use). No more blind concatenation of the raw external path onto a base dir.</li>
                <li>Added a traversal guard: the resolved path must stay inside the repo root, else 400 (mirrors <code>Admin/Git.pm file_diff</code>).</li>
                <li><code>_ai2_repo_rel_path</code> normalization hardened to strip a leading <code>/</code>, <code>Comserv/</code>, <em>and</em> any leading absolute prefix equal to the app dir or repo root, so absolute/over-prefixed frontend paths no longer double up.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="files" class="doc-h2">4. Files changed</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/AI2.pm</code> &mdash; <code>file_diff</code>: path resolved from repo_root + repo_rel, traversal guard; <code>_ai2_repo_rel_path</code>: absolute/over-prefix stripping (uncommitted, pending commit).</li>
                <li>Related (already in place from prior work): <code>lib/Comserv/Util/Git.pm</code> (<code>--no-index</code> allowed), <code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Admin/Git.pm</code> (file_diff logs failures).</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="verify" class="doc-h2">5. Verification</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>perl -Ilib -c lib/Comserv/Controller/AI2.pm</code> &rarr; syntax OK.</li>
                <li>Standalone <code>:3001</code> auto-reloads; the doubled-path case is now impossible because the path is built from the canonical <code>repo_root + repo_rel</code> and confined to the repo root.</li>
                <li>Re-test: click <strong>Diff</strong> on a changed/new file in the AI2 Project panel &mdash; for new files it shows full content as additions; for modified files the vs-HEAD diff.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

</div>
</div>

<div id="2026-08-18-ai-index-tt-render-race" class="cl-entry">
<h3>ai/index.tt &mdash; transient render-time truncation (marked resolved)</h3>
<div class="container">

    <h1 class="doc-h1">ai/index.tt parse error &mdash; not a source defect (render-time race)</h1>

    <div class="last-updated" doc-muted>
        Last Updated: 2026-08-18 | Version: 1.00 | Author: hermes | Status: Resolved &mdash; no code change
    </div>

    <div id="toc" class="row doc-toc">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">Quick Navigation</h2>
            <div class="doc-navrow">
                <a href="#summary" class="doc-navlink">Summary</a>
                <a href="#root" class="doc-navlink">Root cause</a>
                <a href="#evidence" class="doc-navlink">Evidence</a>
                <a href="#verify" class="doc-navlink">Verification</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="summary" class="doc-h2">1. Summary</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">The Application Error Audit todo <code>ai &mdash; Couldn't render template "ai/index.tt: file error - parse error ... unexpected end of input</code> (logged 2026-08-16 from the prod-mirror Docker container on :5000) was diagnosed as a <strong>transient artifact, not a fixable source bug</strong>. The authoritative template is complete and valid; the error cannot be reproduced from it.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="2026-08-19-floating-button-theme-respect-todo" class="cl-entry">
        <h2>2026-08-19 — Floating buttons (Chat with AI + Back-to-Top): theme-respect todo #2160 + plan/doc sync</h2>
        <p><strong>Last Updated:</strong> 2026-08-19 | <strong>Version:</strong> 1.00 | <strong>Author:</strong> hermes | <strong>Status:</strong> Tracked (linked to project #221 THEME-AUDIT; shared with #259 V2MIG)</p>

        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-100">
                <h3 class="doc-h3">What changed</h3>
                <ul class="doc-body">
                    <li>Created todo <a href="/todo/details?record_id=2160" class="doc-link">#2160</a> under <strong>proj #221 Theme Compliance Audit</strong> (cross-referenced to <strong>proj #259 V2MIG</strong> for the V2 JS/CSS migration). Subject: <em>"Floating buttons (Chat with AI + Back-to-Top) ignore theme/placement rules — fix in V2 JS/CSS"</em>.</li>
                    <li>Registered #2160 in <code>Documentation/MASTER_PLAN.tt</code> as a sub-item of the #221 Theme Compliance Audit bullet, with a note that it is distinct from the <code>c6bd92b6</code> zombie-button / duplicate-arrow fix (that was a stale <code>localStorage</code> flag, not placement).</li>
                    <li>Updated <code>Documentation/features/back_to_top.tt</code> to correct the implementation notes (the button is fixed <strong>bottom-LEFT</strong> at <code>bottom:20px;left:20px</code>, not bottom-right as the old doc claimed), document that it is wired by both <code>back-to-top.js</code> and <code>floating-buttons.js</code>, note the removed duplicate <code>.back-to-top</code> injected by <code>todo-enhancements.js</code>, and add a theme-governance callout + Future-Enhancement item pointing at todo #2160.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-100">
                <h3 class="doc-h3">Root cause the todo addresses</h3>
                <ul class="doc-body">
                    <li>The floating <em>Chat with AI</em> (<code>.chat-button</code>) and <code>#back-to-top</code> buttons use hardcoded <code>position:fixed</code> offsets, z-index, and colors (literals, not theme <code>var(--*)</code> tokens). AI-authored edits therefore repeatedly break their placement and collide with the AI2 float button (<code>bottom:90px;left:24px</code>).</li>
                    <li>Forward fix (todo #2160): drive offsets/z-index/colors from theme variables so the theme system controls placement, make the rule survive AI edits without drift, and guarantee no collision with other floating elements.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-100">
                <h3 class="doc-h3">Files touched (documentation only — no code behavior changed)</h3>
                <ul class="doc-body">
                    <li><code>root/Documentation/MASTER_PLAN.tt</code> — #221 bullet extended with todo #2160 sub-item.</li>
                    <li><code>root/Documentation/features/back_to_top.tt</code> — corrected implementation/theme notes + #2160 cross-reference.</li>
                    <li><code>root/Documentation/changelog/CHANGELOG.tt</code> — this entry + TOC anchor.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="doc-note"><strong>Note:</strong> the actual bug fixes (zombie popup-active flag + removal of the injected duplicate <code>.back-to-top</code>) shipped earlier in commit <code>c6bd92b6</code>. This entry only records the planning/documentation sync for the separate theme-respect governance task.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="root" class="doc-h2">2. Root cause</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li>"unexpected end of input at line 34" means the Template Toolkit parser hit EOF while still inside a <code>&#91;% ... %&#93;</code> block &mdash; i.e. the file was <strong>truncated at render time</strong>. This is the classic signature of an edit/deploy race on a running container: a <code>.tt</code> was being written/replaced while the live server reloaded it mid-write and read a half-written copy.</li>
                <li>The error is not a persistent source defect. Nothing in the source changed between the image build and the error, and once the file finished writing the page renders normally.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="evidence" class="doc-h2">3. Evidence</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>root/ai/index.tt</code> currently = 1111 lines, balanced <code>&#91;%/%%&#93;</code> tags, and parses cleanly through Template Toolkit (verified: 37,878-char render, no error).</li>
                <li>The image it was baked from (<code>fbbc501c</code>, built 2026-08-16 01:08, the <code>version.json</code> commit) also has the complete 1111-line file; the only <code>&#91;% PROCESS %&#93;</code> target (<code>ai/model_select.tt</code>) is complete (79 lines).</li>
                <li>Last commit touching <code>ai/index.tt</code> (<code>61c7573c</code>, 2026-08-11) predates the error and is also complete &mdash; so this was not a broken commit that later got fixed.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="verify" class="doc-h2">4. Verification</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li>Template parsed with <code>Template-&gt;new-&gt;process($file, {}, \$out)</code> &rarr; OK (no parse error).</li>
                <li>The container that logged it (<code>workstation-prod-local (Docker):5000</code>) is not currently running in this environment, so it cannot re-error.</li>
                <li>Verdict: no code change required; the source is correct and the parse failure cannot reproduce from it.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <div class="doc-footer">
                <p><em>This is a diagnostic/closure note for an Application Error Audit todo. No files changed.</em></p>
                <p><em>This documentation is part of the Comserv system.</em></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

