<div id="2026-08-17-hermes-branch-context" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-08-17 — Hermes Branch Context system</h3>
<div class="container">
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <p class="doc-muted">Last Updated: 2026-08-17 | Version: 0.1 | Tracked in project: <a href="/project/details?project_id=238" class="doc-link">#238 (GITWT-NEW)</a>. Folded here from a standalone dated changelog file (policy: single CHANGELOG.tt).</p>
            <h4 class="doc-h3">What changed</h4>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Branch <code>.hermes.md</code> domain files</strong> written for the then-6 existing worktrees: InventoryAccounting, 3d, DockerHA, ai, aichatsystem-ef4e, git. Each re-includes the global <code>/home/shanta/PycharmProjects/comserv2/.hermes.md</code> then adds domain expertise. BMaster (beekeeping) deferred until its worktree exists. Status later corrected on 2026-08-19 (files were not actually on disk until then; planning added).</li>
                <li><strong>Git dashboard &quot;Hermes&quot; button</strong> — <code>Util/Git.pm -&gt; build_worktree_list</code> emits <code>hermes_cmd</code>; <code>root/admin/git/index.tt</code> adds the button (and fixes Open to use an absolute <code>scheme://host:port/path</code> URL); <code>root/static/js/git-dashboard.js</code> copies the command to clipboard. Later corrected: do not copy <code>hermes chat -w</code> (that flag nests a <code>hermes/hermes-*</code> scratch branch).</li>
                <li><strong>Planning plan doc</strong> — <a href="/Documentation/HermesBranchContextPlan" class="doc-link">/Documentation/HermesBranchContextPlan</a>, tracked under #238 with todos 2142–2146 (2146 recurring re-audit, set recurrence in the Todo UI).</li>
                <li><strong>MASTER_PLAN</strong> — new index row + &quot;Hermes Context&quot; navlink; back-links added from the sibling git-worktree plans.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-body">Why: each worktree is its own git root, so Hermes does not inherit the repo-root global rules. Related: <a href="/Documentation/HermesBranchContextPlan" class="doc-link">Hermes Branch Context Plan</a>, <a href="/Documentation/CHANGELOG#2026-08-19-hermes-branch-context-authoring" class="doc-link">2026-08-19 authoring correction</a>.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</div>

<div id="2026-08-19-ai-index-tt-parse-retry" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-08-19 — ai/index.tt unexpected-EOF: retry truncated TT compile</h3>
<div class="container">
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <p class="doc-body">Application Error Audit todo <a href="/todo/details?record_id=2147" class="doc-link">#2147</a> (site 3d, <code>workstation-prod-local:5000</code>, 114 hits) is <code>Couldn't render template "ai/index.tt ... line 34: unexpected end of input"</code>. The on-disk template is complete (1111 lines) and compiles. The live :5000 compose bind-mounts <code>./Comserv</code> over <code>/opt/comserv</code>, so a request that compiles the file mid-save reads a half-written copy. Earlier diagnosis closed this as non-reproducible; it kept firing.</p>
            <p class="doc-body"><strong>Fix:</strong> <code>Comserv::View::TT::render</code> retries once after 150ms + TT cache reset when the error is this truncation class. Recovered races log <code>warning</code>; a still-broken template logs <code>error</code> and rethrows (audit trail kept). No change to <code>root/ai/index.tt</code> (already over the 1000-line soft target; source is valid).</p>
            <p class="doc-body">Files: <code>lib/Comserv/View/TT.pm</code>, <code>t/view_TT.t</code>. Verify: <code>prove -l t/view_TT.t</code>.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</div>

<div id="2026-08-19-focus-queue-p1-trust" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-08-19 — Focus Queue ranks trusted blockers, not inflated P1s</h3>
<div class="container">
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <p class="doc-muted">Last Updated: 2026-08-19 | Tracked: <a href="/todo/details?record_id=1828" class="doc-link">#1828 PLAN-QUEUE Ph4</a> / <a href="/todo/details?record_id=1817" class="doc-link">#1817 priority triage</a>.</p>
            <p class="doc-body">The Focus Queue and /todo list ranked on stored <code>priority</code>. ~248 active rows are still P1, so real work (and any honest P2/P3) sat at rank ~200. Agents were gaming due dates and moving phase todos onto the parent project so they could appear. That is the wrong layer.</p>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>P1 trust:</strong> <code>TodoRanking</code> now scores a stored P1 as P5 unless <code>is_blocking</code> is set or the subject/description is a real incident (<code>[Error]</code>, outage, merge conflict, cannot restore, etc.). Displayed priority is unchanged.</li>
                <li><strong>Reschedule does not refresh freshness.</strong> Staleness uses <code>date_time_posted</code> when <code>last_mod_by=reschedule</code>.</li>
                <li><strong>Recent incidents</strong> get an extra boost so today's error todos beat planned work without rewriting due dates.</li>
                <li><strong>Project filter includes children.</strong> <code>filter_project=272</code> (DRYER-INT) now includes phase projects whose <code>parent_id</code> is 272. No need to reparent todos.</li>
                <li><strong>Per-project cap</strong> of half the Focus Queue (#1828 F5) so one project cannot fill all 20 slots.</li>
                <li><strong>No lunch / appointments in Daily Priorities.</strong> Breaks are created as <code>is_fixed</code> tasks (not <code>todo_type=appointment</code>), so the old type filter missed them. <code>TodoTypes::is_calendar_fixture</code> now drops appointments, meetings, events, reminders, and any subject matching lunch/break/standup. They stay on the calendar.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-body"><strong>AI assist:</strong> do not ask an LLM to sort 1000 rows on every page load. <code>GET /api/focus/top5</code> already re-ranks the <em>top 50 by ap_score</em>. This scorer change is what makes that candidate pool honest. Stored-priority cleanup remains <a href="/todo/details?record_id=1817" class="doc-link">#1817</a> (batch, local Ollama).</p>
            <p class="doc-body">Files: <code>lib/Comserv/Util/TodoRanking.pm</code>, <code>lib/Comserv/Util/FocusRanking.pm</code>, <code>lib/Comserv/Util/TodoTypes.pm</code>, <code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Planning.pm</code>, <code>t/util_todo_ranking.t</code>.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</div>

<div id="2026-08-19-hermes-no-nested-worktree" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-08-19 — Git dashboard Hermes launch must not use -w</h3>
<div class="container">
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <p class="doc-body">The Git dashboard Develop Servers &quot;Hermes&quot; button copied <code>hermes chat -w</code>. That flag creates a nested <code>hermes/hermes-*</code> worktree + branch (often from <code>origin/main</code>), so the agent is not on the feature branch the user clicked. Comserv already isolates via <code>~/.comserv/worktrees/&lt;branch&gt;/Comserv</code>.</p>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>Util::Git-&gt;build_worktree_list</code> now emits <code>cd &lt;git-root&gt; &amp;&amp; hermes chat</code> (no <code>-w</code>) for <code>main</code> and every registered branch.</li>
                <li>Plan + 3d branch context updated: never launch Hermes with <code>-w</code> from a Comserv worktree.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-body">Files: <code>lib/Comserv/Util/Git.pm</code>, <code>root/static/js/git-dashboard.js</code>, <code>root/Documentation/HermesBranchContextPlan.tt</code>. Tracked under <a href="/todo/details?record_id=2143" class="doc-link">todo #2143</a> / project <a href="/project/details?project_id=238" class="doc-link">#238 GITWT-NEW</a>.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</div>

